[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_1]
Half-Remembered Dream I: A Normal Day

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_1_desc]
The recent news had cast a shadow over the entire Pie family, though it had been that way for a while. This brought back memories for Maud Pie, of a typical day last year...

§bIt was another busy day at the Rock Farm. Maudalina Daisy Pie, or Maud Pie as she was known, stepped out of the recently finished meeting hall. Her sister, Limestone Pie, remained inside with several managerial ponies from Pondrosa and Rockville, discussing the Rock Farm’s weekly supply quotas.Marble Pie was already tending to their parents — Igneous Rock and Cloudy Quartz, at the farm’s hospital. Both were bedridden and required constant care. Maud Pie made her way slowly to the pride of the Pie family, Holder’s Boulder, carefully wiping it clean. Busy ponies passed by, greeting her as they went.
Not long ago, this had been barren land with nothing but a small two-story house, a windmill, and a stone silo. Now, thousands of ponies called this place home, with tents and low buildings scattered across the landscape.Luckily, the minerals and stones in the land could be exchanged via rail with cities like Manehattan and Appleloosa for the necessities of life. Despite the harsh winter winds, life was relatively comfortable here compared to the more distant regions, where survival itself was a luxury.
Maud’s gaze fell upon a rundown building, their former shared residence. It had been a while since they’d slept there together, given their busy schedules. After finishing with Holder’s Boulder, Maud walked towards it, the wooden boards creaking under her hooves. The house needed to be cleaned thoroughly to serve as a temporary hospital for more refugees and possible mothers-to-be. Its sturdy reinforced walls could withstand the biting cold. Though the Pie family preferred to leave it as a memorial to bygone days, having more lives sheltered during harsh winters was a consolation. Maud didn’t mind other ponies staying in their old house, but she missed one room in particular—the room belonging to her sister, the always cheerful Pinkie Pie, who would wake up early every day to prepare surprises for her.
Entering that room, Maud sat quietly, away from the noise of the outside world, savoring every moment. The winter sun cast its light upon Maud’s dull gray coat, almost like Pinkie Pie’s gentle touch. Despite maintaining her usual impassive demeanor, a slight downturn at the corner of her mouth betrayed her true feelings. Any pony familiar with her would know that was her saddest moment.§!

But no matter how hopeless things seemed at the time, life was still full of hope, unlike now.
It was on that day that she found the small wooden box that would change the Pie family forever—a gift Pinkie Pie had left behind before she disappeared...

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_1_o0]
“I miss you...”

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_2]
Half-Remembered Dream II: Accidental Discovery

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_2_desc]
§bMaud Pie began sorting through the clutter in the room, preparing to move it to the nearby stone silo. However, one box hidden behind the bed board caught her attention.
Pinkie Pie’s hiding skills were impressive, as she had never seen it before. Carefully wiping off the dust, a line of text on the box made Maud  break into a rare smile: “For the best sister, Maud Pie”
She opened the small box, and a cascade of ribbons burst out from the triggered mechanism, accompanied by joyful sounds, sprinkling over Maud Pie. Inside the box, it contained a variety of items that far exceeded the box’s capacity: fireworks, greeting cards, some drafts of unknown significance, and even balloons — inflated.
Maud Pie raised an eyebrow slightly, her expression did not change much, as always, without saying a word. She stayed alone in the room for a long time, thinking of a friend that Pinkie Pie had mentioned many times, a pony who was as crazy and whimsical as her — Cheese Sandwich.§!

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_2_o0]
Thank you, Pinkie Pie

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_3]
Half-Remembered Dream III: Cheese Sandwich

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_3_desc]
§bFrom Cloud City to Manehattan, as one of the few things that could bring smiles nowadays, toys named after him held an unshakeable place in the hearts of foals and some adult ponies. But no matter how many toys and factories existed, they couldn’t bring even a hint of real joy to Cheese Sandwich himself. With the advent of the Last Roundup, freedom became history, and his beloved Pinkie Pie had disappeared, though he had never confessed his feelings to her. Equestria was under the control of a figure named Cozy Glow, while giant centaurs and shape-shifters wreaked havoc everywhere. Few ordinary ponies were in the mood for parties anymore, and no matter how much profit the newly minted aristocrats derived from Cozy Glow’s rule, he would always refuse their requests, thanks to the diligent work of his assistant manager, Sans Smirk, and some necessary bribes, Joyful Enterprises still operated, helping as many ponies as possible find joy or work and selling products in more areas.
Now, Cheese Sandwich still spent most of his time traveling across Equestria, offering solace to ponies in need whenever he could, but life’s hardships weren’t solved by a few parties or jokes. As he traveled through White Tail Woods today, his tail twitched uncontrollably six times, followed by two twitches of his mane, indicating one thing.§!

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_3_o0]
“Let’s go, Boneless, Rock Farm need our help.”

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_4]
Half-Remembered Dream IV: Mysterious Draft

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_4_desc]
§bMaud Pie felt a slight surprise. She had expected to wait for weeks before receiving a response from Cheese Sandwich via Amusement Integration, but here he was, standing before her with such seriousness.
Maud raised an eyebrow slightly, when Cheese Sandwich, with a stalk of barley held between his teeth, began to speak: “Oh, don’t be so surprised, dear. Boneless told me you were having some trouble, so I came over.” He said, gesturing towards the squawking rubber chicken on his back.
Maud Pie brought Cheese Sandwich over to the small box and presented him with the sketches and messy drawings, treating them as she would her most precious pet rocks.
Cheese Sandwich’s eyes betrayed a hint of sadness. “Regardless of whether these have any practical significance, I believe they are what she considered most precious.”
Cheese Sandwich began to study the sketches continuously. In the early days of Amusement Factory, he had drawn many similar things. Though Pinkie Pie’s drawings appeared chaotic on the surface, they actually contained meticulous details, mostly upgrades to her party props. For instance, the improved party cannon, which, even with ammunition changed from fireworks to iron shells, could achieve ranges and firing speeds previously unimaginable. Similar upgrades were made to hot air balloons and other items. Pinkie Pie’s original intention maybe was to use them for even more thrilling parties. Alongside the structural drawings were her hopes for the future, especially regarding Maud Pie and Mudbriar’s wedding party. Pinkie Pie’s handwriting became ecstatic at the mention of this, though whenever she brought up Cheese Sandwich, she would abruptly stop, as if holding back something.
In any case, these items could be applied to other areas effectively, enough to rejuvenate the entire Rock Farm. After listening to Cheese Sandwich’s explanation, Maud Pie felt a glimmer of hope. Previously, she had envisioned a plan even larger than Holder’s Boulder in her mind, but disappointment in the future had prevented her from committing to it. Now, with Pinkie Pie’s encouragement and assistance, she found the motivation to revitalize her spirits.§!

... It has been over a year since then, and the Rock Farm has changed from a small family that barely made a living by mining ore, to a military industry with a large number of orders. Indeed, the small wooden box left by her sister was the last gift she left to the family... When did she leave the box? This may not be important. Now that we have lost the genius designer, we are still here, continuing her dream. Although we sell fear and gunfire, the blood-stained bits of money have fed our families, countless hungry refugee ponies, and those creatures who have lost their homes in the flames of war.
Is it worth it? Maud Pie doesn’t know, she just hopes that the “Element of Laughter” can once again come to this land.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_4_o0]
Time to convene a family meeting to implement the reform plan for the rock farm.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_5]
Family meeting

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_5_desc]
As Maud Pie entered the meeting room, carrying copies of Pinkie’s drawings, Limestone Pie, Marble Pie, and Mudbriar sat waiting for her in the cramped space.
A year ago, their family members had gathered here to discuss plans for the future. During the meeting, Maud Pie presented her family members with a plan for the future regarding the Pie family’s control over the region, encompassing various industries. Though implementing it would be extremely challenging, if it could improve the lives of the ponies living on this barren land, then it would all be worthwhile.
Now, the Pie family members had gathered once again to discuss plans for the future, hoping to improve the lives of the ponies living on this barren land.
Practice has proven that it is worthwhile.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_5_o0]
Let’s do it! For Pinkie and the other ponies!

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_6]
Maud pie’s speech

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_6_desc]
On a bright morning, Maud Pie ascended the makeshift podium. The seats below were filled with representatives from across the autonomous territory. As Maud Pie cleared her throat, the audience gradually quieted down. She began, “Ponies of the autonomous territory, I am Maud Pie. Just a few years ago, our farm was like limestone, but now we have become conglomerate. Just as I met my boulder, I have told this story before, on a stormy night. At that time, I had no idea that life would change forever. We didn’t believe we were capable of leading you; we tried to leave, but we stayed. Just as rocks are strong, the ponies on this land will be strong. Some new initiatives will be implemented to help everyone become even stronger. To this end, I have written a poem for everyone”. She then started the following poem:

“Rocks, these are my rocks.
Sediments make me sedimental.
depth, shallowness, like hearts, intertwined,
Deep, asleep, merging, changing.

Rocks, these are my rocks.
Quartzite, we’re forever united.”

Copies of the speech were distributed throughout the autonomous territory using duplication magic, to cater to those without radios or lacking a bit of patience. One copy was also placed on the desk of the Ministry of Order of the Equestria Empire to analyze whether Maud Pie’s words held any hidden meaning.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_6_o0]
As expected of a pony with rocktorate...

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_7]
Wooden Fossil Exhibition

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_7_desc]
On this sunny morning, representatives from across the autonomy and curious onlookers gathered at the exhibition square of the farm. Maud Pie and Mudbriar had spent over a month preparing for this, setting up exhibition facilities and transporting precious fossils. Mudbriar stood on a platform, meticulously introducing each item to be displayed. Meanwhile, the shy Marble Pie had hidden herself away, while the cautious Limestone Pie stood amidst the crowd, casting vigilant glances at any pony exhibiting suspicious behavior. After a long hour of introductions, Mudbriar finally declared the exhibition open. The sleepy ponies suddenly perked up, bursting into enthusiastic applause, and began to enter the exhibition hall to view these fossils they couldn’t understand.
Following the conclusion of the exhibition, a small pony folk band performed the new song “Rock Anthem” written by Maud Pie. Whether genuine or not, most ponies present still gave the exhibition favorable reviews, though perhaps more credit was due to the unlimited supply of apple cider available at the event.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_7_o0]
At least it turned out well...

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_8]
Train Trip

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_8_desc]
Maud Pie, Mudbriar, Marble Pie, and some newly appointed officials from the rock farm boarded the train, nodding to Limestone Pie who remained on the platform. Someone had to manage the autonomy in the days the delegation was away on their visit. The train departed from the Big Thunder Mine, heading towards the western outskirts of Appleloosa at the train station. Along the way, the train passed by the two Sisters’ Castle. Not much had changed about the castle: the dense forest grew unchecked, with broken stones and weeds scattered about as they had been for years. However, the tallest tower of the castle still stood, gradually appearing in Maud Pie’s distant view. What would things be like now if the Ultimate Battle hadn’t happened? What would happen to the rock farm and Appleloosa? Would Pinkie Pie come back? Many questions flooded Maud Pie’s mind, leaving her feeling a bit restless.
“I don’t mean to pry, but it seems like you have something on your mind. Judging by where our train is currently, you’re probably reminiscing about the past. I’m deeply sorry for that”, Mudbriar spoke, choosing his words carefully, showing genuine concern. However, Maud Pie just looked at her fiancé, calmly stating “I’m fine” before turning back to gaze out the window, lost in thought.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_8_o0]
No time for nostalgia, Maud pie...

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_9]
Meeting with Braeburn

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_9_desc]
As the train whistles faded, the restless trains gradually settled, and as soon as the doors opened, they were greeted by an energetic cowboy-dressed stallion, beaming a broad smile at them. The stallion, named Braeburn, exclaimed, “Welcome to Appaloosa, my good kinfolk! Let’s sing it out, Apple family folks!”
With his face turned towards his band, Braeburn continued to smile broadly, shouting, “Well done, folks!” to them, before whispering to Maud Pie, “I’ve strengthened security and surveillance. Cozy Glow’s lackeys won’t find it easy to get close to us.”
Maud Pie scrutinized his face; compared to their first meeting years ago, he seemed a bit older now, and his previous smile held a hint of falsity and sorrow. Whether Pie family ponies or Apple family ponies, they all drifted like lone boats on a stormy sea in these dark times, but Maud Pie didn’t acknowledge this.

After the welcome ceremony, Maud Pie, Braeburn, and other ponies headed towards the administrative building of the autonomous territory. A black-and-white portrait caught Marble Pie’s attention, and tears uncontrollably streamed down her cheeks. She had once fallen for an Appleloosa stallion but never dared to express her feelings. It led to a mare from the distant town of Equality winning his heart, and he vanished without a trace in a mysterious accident. Yet, Marble Pie’s delicate heart still harbored a small pang of regret.
By evening, Maud Pie led a delegation from the quarry farm and Braeburn’s representatives from Appleloosa in negotiations. A series of deeper mutual assistance treaties were signed or renewed, and the possibility of future mergers between the two prominent families was even discussed. However, this would surely raise alarms and opposition from the Equestria Empire, so caution was necessary. Additionally, there were the Las Pegasus, the notorious brothers with complex ties to the Apple family. The brothers surely had devised countless schemes to control both the rock farm and Appleloosa. If the quarry farm and Appaloosa were to join forces to Las Pegasus’s trade routes completely, it would be utterly unacceptable for Las Pegasus.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_9_o0]
Bond between the two families must not be broken

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_10]
Machine Outage

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_10_desc]
Overnight, many of our factories’ machines ceased operation. Our industrial sector immediately organized engineers to investigate. Unexpectedly, Amusement Factory and some facilities constructed entirely by ourselves remained operational. All the malfunctioning machines had originated from Las Pegasus or had excessively utilized blueprints and parts from Las Pegasus. An urgent telegram was dispatched to Las Pegasus demanding an explanation, but all we received in return was mockery from the Flim and Flam brothers and a request for a face-to-face meeting. It was clear that they had orchestrated this major incident. Despite warnings from Appleloosa about the twins’ profit-driven nature, our rapid economic growth had caused us to relax our vigilance. Now, we were forced to confront difficult choices.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_10_o0]
Pie family will resolve this crisis...

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_11]
Negotiate with the Twins

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_11_desc]
“Don’t you dare to break ground on tuff rock!”

Limestone Pie slammed her hoof down heavily on the table, sending wood splinters flying. A large crack formed along the table, pointing accusingly at the two brothers, causing Flam to wisely shut his mouth just as he was about to speak.
“What is tuff rock?” Flam whispered to his elder brother, but Flim was too preoccupied to respond to Flam. Summoning his courage, Flim shouted back at Limestone Pie: “Actually, it was voluntary on your part!”
Flim cleared his throat, buying himself a couple of seconds of composure, and continued, “You willingly accepted our offer of heavily discounted machinery, full sets of blueprints, and other documents, even rejecting the assistance of the Apple family as a result. I regret that, but I assure you that your decisions were both worthwhile and as beneficial as you initially perceived.”

Limestone Pie was about to explode, but Maud Pie signaled for her to calm down. In a calm and quiet voice, Maud explained, "We should have realized their true intentions long ago. Braeburn reminded us of this, but It’s too late to argue with them now.”
Upon hearing this, the two brothers exchanged glances, their faces showing a sense of triumph. Gradually, they remembered that they were the ones leading today’s meeting. Limestone Pie looked towards the two brothers and asked, “If today can still be considered negotiation, what are your terms?”
Flam looked smugly at Limestone Pie and said, “It’s simple. As indispensable investors and developers for the rock farm, we should have control over monthly finances, dividends, and partial rights to external trade. And if you don’t mind, more industrial equipment developed by Las Pegasus is already on its way here.”

After a moment of contemplation, Maud Pie responded slowly:

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_11_o0]
“We accept your terms.”

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_11_o1]
“Don’t you even think about it.”

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_12]
Investment to Rock Farm

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_12_desc]
Our cooperation with the rock farm has yielded further results. Many companies from the rock farm have come to Appleloosa seeking opportunities, leading to the establishment of more factories.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_12_o0]
Here’s to our kinship!

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_13]
Ponies Initiated Protests!

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_13_desc]
Coincidentally, just before this earthquake occurred, we had recently built some brand-new radar stations near Rockville. Many ponies at the rock farm had never seen anything like them before, and they stubbornly linked the radar stations to the earthquake, believing that these strange machines caused it. Now, the gates of Rockville’s government hall are surrounded by protesting ponies, demanding that we immediately dismantle the radar stations, or they will continue protesting indefinitely.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_13_o0]
It’s simply unreasonable. We won’t dismantle our radar tower.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_13_o1]
Let the will of the ponies be done, even if it’s not always right.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_14]
Second Batch of Sponsorship

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_14_desc]
Las Pegasus has once again offered us extensive assistance in many aspects, primarily focusing on our mining and heavy industries. A variety of equipment manufactured in Las Pegasus is being loaded onto trains, awaiting transport to our farm. While one might occasionally interpret this as charity from Las Pegasus, their commercial nature proves they undoubtedly have ulterior motives. Appleloosa also telegrammed us upon learning of this. The rulers of Las Pegasus, the Flim and Flam brothers, have repeatedly attempted to deceive important members of the Apple family and plotted against the prized apple orchards.

If we were to switch to cooperation with Appleloosa now, perhaps we wouldn’t receive such generous support anymore, but we wouldn’t have to speculate about Las Pegasus’ true intentions. Of course, accepting this aid is clearly more advantageous for the quarry farm. We can investigate Las Pegasus’ intentions later, and abruptly ending the cooperation would undoubtedly incur retaliation from the Flim Flam brothers.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_14_o0]
We’ll play along for now and see what they have in mind later.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_14_o1]
Whatever their true intentions are, they won’t succeed.

[en.PIHC_COUNTRY_FLAG_C12_ACCEPT_SECOND_BATCH_OF_SPONSORSHIP_TOOLTIP]
Accept the second batch of sponsorship from Las Pegasus.

[en.PIHC_COUNTRY_FLAG_C12_REFUSE_SECOND_BATCH_OF_SPONSORSHIP_TOOLTIP]
Refuse the second batch of sponsorship from Las Pegasus.

[en.PIHC_COUNTRY_FLAG_C12_ACCEPT_SECOND_BATCH_OF_SPONSORSHIP_TRIGGER_TOOLTIP]
We have accepted the second batch of sponsorship from Las Pegasus.

[en.PIHC_COUNTRY_FLAG_C12_REFUSE_SECOND_BATCH_OF_SPONSORSHIP_TRIGGER_TOOLTIP]
We have refused our cooperation with Las Pegasus.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_15]
Cloudsdale Agreement

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_15_desc]
A representative from the rock farm appeared in front of Derpy Hooves.
To be able to ascend to Cloudsdale in the sky, this earth pony envoy, who had never looked up at the sky in his life, almost scared himself to death.
Derpy didn’t know where the rock farm was, but she learned from the envoy that as long as she signed her name on this paper, she could eat the special stone muffins from the rock farm. At the same time, the agreement has been approved by the lower officials, and there will be no loss to Cloudsdale.
So without much thought, Derpy nodded and hurriedly ended her morning work. It’s lunchtime!

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_15_o0]
So are stone muffins really edible?

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_16]
Cloudsdale Agreement

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_16_desc]
A representative from the rock farm appeared in front of Derpy Hooves.
To be able to ascend to Cloudsdale in the sky, this earth pony envoy, who had never looked up at the sky in his life, almost scared himself to death.
Derpy didn’t know where the rock farm was, but she learned from the envoy that as long as she signed her name on this paper, she could eat the special stone muffins from the rock farm. At the same time, the agreement has been approved by the lower officials, and there will be no loss to Cloudsdale.
The content of the agreement is probably that Cloudsdale sends experts to the rock farm to help them establish or improve the air force, and the rock farm provides us with economic support and stone muffins.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_16_o0]
Rock cupcakes? What would they taste like? I have to try one!

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_16_o1]
Stone muffins sound as bad as stones themselves!

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_16_TOOLTIP]
§Y[C12.GetName]§! will provide us with §Y50§! muffins each month.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_17]
Cloudsdale Agreement

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_17_desc]
A representative from the rock farm appeared in front of Derpy Hooves.
To be able to ascend to Cloudsdale in the sky, this earth pony envoy, who had never looked up at the sky in his life, almost scared himself to death.
Derpy didn’t know where the rock farm was, but she learned from the envoy that as long as she signed her name on this paper, she could eat the special stone muffins from the rock farm. At the same time, the agreement has been approved by the lower officials, and there will be no loss to Cloudsdale.
However, Derpy Hooves, in an unusual turn of events, expressed no interest in the stone muffins. Although the lower officials wanted to facilitate the conclusion of this agreement, if Derpy did not approve it, it seemed that the matter would have to be shelved.
Originally, the envoy and the officials wanted to persuade her, but it was lunchtime. Everypony knows that there is nothing more important than Duchess Derpy’s lunchtime.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_17_o0]
Can’t you just use regular muffins? You idiots!

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_18]
Apple Pie Integration Agreement

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_18_desc]
The Apple and Pie families recently held a collective wedding: all the couples among the offspring of both families who have not yet dated will get married at the same time at this collective wedding.
At the wedding, the leaders of both families signed an agreement to ensure the eternal friendship of the two families. This agreement is called the “Apple Pie Integration Agreement”, which will officially merge the two families into one.
This is a historic moment.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_18_o0]
Okay

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_18_o1]
To Friendship!

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_18_o2]
To Friendship!

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_19]
Cooperative Development

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_19_desc]
The rich mineral deposits recently discovered at the rock farm have attracted attention from various factions. However, due to our lack of facilities and funds, we may not be able to utilize them effectively for a long time, unless we choose to cooperate with other countries. Currently, we have two main options before us:
First is the region of Appleloosa, controlled by our relatives, the Apple family. Over the years, we have built a deep friendship with them and spent many Hearth’s Warming Eves together. However, the heavy wars have torn apart the entire world and the Apple family as well: important family members such as Big Mac and Applejack have gone missing, leaving Appleloosa in a state of decline that has yet to fully recover. Nevertheless, if we need help, we believe they will provide enthusiastic assistance.
The other option is the emerging region of Las Pegasus, controlled by the Flim and Flam brothers. With the push of these two inventors and capitalists, who have quite a mixed reputation, Las Pegasus has become the technological and economic center of the entire continent. Only a few regions like Sire’s Hollow can rival Las Pegasus in grandeur, but behind this is the brothers’ insatiable greed. If we seek cooperation with them, they will certainly agree and offer us much more favorable conditions, but they will also have other demands of us.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_19_o0]
Charity begins at home

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_19_o1]
Business is business

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_20]
Rock Farm Seeks Cooperation

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_20_desc]
Our neighboring rock farm has long been considered barren land, with many ponies struggling to make ends meet. However, not long ago, their leader, Maud Pie, organized a large-scale geological exploration activity for the entire autonomous territory. Many valuable minerals were discovered, but their capacity to utilize them effectively is lacking. In order to develop their economy, the rock farm has surprisingly extended a priority cooperation invitation to us, inviting us to their land. If we can come up with the right approach, we could seize this opportunity to claim their assets and wealth as our own, incorporating them into our sphere of influence.

Hey there! We’ve actually been brainstorming a new invention... What if you say, we install special key components in our machines that will automatically expire after a certain period of time? If they want to continue using those machines, they’ll have to rely on us for replacements. At that point, the price will be entirely up to us...
We can use this to devise a brilliant plan! When our machines are spread across the rock farm’s land, the Pie family won’t be able to refuse any of our requests unless they want the rock farm’s economy to collapse completely.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_20_o0]
Nothing more expensive than something free!

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_20_o1]
Better not mess with a family running military industry...

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_21]
Las Pegasus Refused Us

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_21_desc]
To our surprise, Las Pegasus actually refused our cooperation invitation, citing a lack of relevant equipment and interest. Now, we have no other choice but to continue cooperating with the Apple family.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_21_o0]
Maybe it’s not such a bad thing...

[en.PIHC_COUNTRY_FLAG_C12_C07_REFUSED_CORPORATION_TRIGGER_TOOLTIP]
Las Pegasus refused the cooperation invitation.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_22]
Las Pegasus Accepted!

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_22_desc]
Las Pegasus has agreed to our development invitation, and the Flim and Flam brothers have shown great interest in our rock farm. They have offered us generous terms, promising us a large amount of machinery for free once we sign the cooperation agreement. Additionally, we only need to pay a reasonable proportion of our earnings.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_22_o0]
Let’s get started right away.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_23]
Anticipated Conflict

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_23_desc]
“Don’t you dare to break ground on tuff rock!”

Limestone Pie slammed her hoof down heavily on the table, sending wood splinters flying. A large crack formed along the table, pointing accusingly at the two brothers, causing Flam to wisely shut his mouth just as he was about to speak.
“What is tuff rock?” Flam whispered to his elder brother, but Flim was too preoccupied to respond to Flam. Summoning his courage, Flim shouted back at Limestone Pie: “Actually, it was voluntary on your part!”
Flim cleared his throat, buying himself a couple of seconds of composure, and continued, “You willingly accepted our offer of heavily discounted machinery, full sets of blueprints, and other documents, even rejecting the assistance of the Apple family as a result. I regret that, but I assure you that your decisions were both worthwhile and as beneficial as you initially perceived.”

Limestone Pie was about to explode, but Maud Pie signaled for her to calm down. In a calm and quiet voice, Maud explained, "We should have realized their true intentions long ago. Braeburn reminded us of this, but It’s too late to argue with them now.”
Upon hearing this, the two brothers exchanged glances, their faces showing a sense of triumph. Gradually, they remembered that they were the ones leading today’s meeting. Limestone Pie looked towards the two brothers and asked, “If today can still be considered negotiation, what are your terms?”
Flam looked smugly at Limestone Pie and said, “It’s simple. As indispensable investors and developers for the rock farm, we should have control over monthly finances, dividends, and partial rights to external trade. And if you don’t mind, more industrial equipment developed by Las Pegasus is already on its way here.”

After a moment of contemplation, Maud Pie responded slowly:
“Don’t you even think about it.”

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_23_o0]
Then wait and see how Las Pegasus does business.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_24]
Anticipated Conflict

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_24_desc]
“Don’t you dare to break ground on tuff rock!”

Limestone Pie slammed her hoof down heavily on the table, sending wood splinters flying. A large crack formed along the table, pointing accusingly at the two brothers, causing Flam to wisely shut his mouth just as he was about to speak.
“What is tuff rock?” Flam whispered to his elder brother, but Flim was too preoccupied to respond to Flam. Summoning his courage, Flim shouted back at Limestone Pie: “Actually, it was voluntary on your part!”
Flim cleared his throat, buying himself a couple of seconds of composure, and continued, “You willingly accepted our offer of heavily discounted machinery, full sets of blueprints, and other documents, even rejecting the assistance of the Apple family as a result. I regret that, but I assure you that your decisions were both worthwhile and as beneficial as you initially perceived.”

Limestone Pie was about to explode, but Maud Pie signaled for her to calm down. In a calm and quiet voice, Maud explained, "We should have realized their true intentions long ago. Braeburn reminded us of this, but It’s too late to argue with them now.”
Upon hearing this, the two brothers exchanged glances, their faces showing a sense of triumph. Gradually, they remembered that they were the ones leading today’s meeting. Limestone Pie looked towards the two brothers and asked, “If today can still be considered negotiation, what are your terms?”
Flam looked smugly at Limestone Pie and said, “It’s simple. As indispensable investors and developers for the rock farm, we should have control over monthly finances, dividends, and partial rights to external trade. And if you don’t mind, more industrial equipment developed by Las Pegasus is already on its way here.”

After a moment of contemplation, Maud Pie responded slowly:
“We accept your terms.”

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_24_o0]
She’s really a pleasure to work with, isn’t she?

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_25]
Retribution of Las Pegasus

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_25_desc]
“Machinery doesn’t exist.”

After the meeting, Las Pegasus suspended the aid agreement with the rock farm, and withdrew all the mechanical maintenance ponies stationed at the rock farm. At first, all ponies thought this was just a normal failed negotiation, until it became closely related to every machine on the rock farm.

If a mineral refiner, with five rough crystal ores put in, spits out five crystals with higher purity extracted from the ores, that is a normal operation of the machine. But imagine another result: the first time, the machine spits out coal after the crystal ores are put in; the second time, the machine spits out nothing; the third time, the ores fly to the ceiling; the fourth time, the machine spits out a muffin that flies around the room and finally dives into your pocket; the fifth time, the ores fly out at nearly the speed of light, smashing a hole in the machine, piercing the wall, and then flying out of the room. What would you think then?

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_25_o0]
“Damn you! Flim and Flam!”

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_26]
Rock Farm Refused!

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_26_desc]
Today, when we were supposed to continue transporting our specialized machinery to the rock farm, patrolling soldiers from the rock farm intercepted our train and informed us that the agreement had been canceled. Perhaps the Pie family discovered something, or maybe it was due to distrust towards us. Nevertheless, our investment cannot be wasted in vain. We must be compensated for our losses from them.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_26_o0]
Every gift from Las Pegasus has already been marked with a price in secret.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_27]
Rock Farm Remains Oblivious

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_27_desc]
Today, under our persuasion, rock farm has once again received a shipment of our machinery. With the roar of the machines, a large quantity of minerals is being extracted, while the Pie family remains in the dark.
Now, our machines are scattered throughout the entire farm. When the time comes for us to reveal our hand, they will have no grounds to challenge us and will have no choice but to accept all our conditions obediently.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_27_o0]
Well down!

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_28]
Cooperative development

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_28_desc]
We have achieved preliminary victories in the war against the rock farm, and their forces are gradually retreating. However, prolonged warfare is not conducive to our economic development, and other factions may intervene in this avoidable conflict. As long as we don’t push the Pie family to the brink, perhaps they will agree to sign a ceasefire treaty. The key question now is what price we should demand.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_28_o0]
Pie family cede Western Equestria to us and compensate for all our losses in this war.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_28_o1]
Limestone Pie actually had the audacity to speak disrespectfully to us before, suggesting that she marry with the Flim Flam brothers to ease tensions between two nations.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_28_o2]
Fully occupying the rock farm is the most prudent choice.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_29]
Las Pegasus demands our surrender

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_29_desc]
The army of Las Pegasus is currently unstoppable on the battlefield, and our current situation is very unfavorable. However, fortunately, the Flim Flam brothers have still expressed the possibility of peace talks. They have stated that as long as we cede West Equestria and repay all losses incurred in this war, they will consider stopping the war, thus sparing the ponies of the rock farm from further conflict.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_29_o0]
We have no other choice but to agree.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_29_o1]
We will not give up until the battle is fought to the last soldier!

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_30]
Las Pegasus demands our surrender

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_30_desc]
Las Pegasus’ army is currently dominating the battlefield, and our current situation is very unfavorable. However, thankfully, the Flim Flam brothers have still expressed the possibility of peace talks. But their conditions are surprisingly...

When Limestone Pie heard this news, she was shocked and paralyzed in her seat. Normally seen as cold-hearted by other ponies, she now appeared tearful, like a little girl. Just the thought of the Flim Flam brothers’ ugly, greedy faces made Limestone Pie seethe with anger. Perhaps at this moment, they were leering over her photos and imagining themselves riding on her. Maud Pie, upon learning of this, attempted to comfort her sister, but didn’t know how to articulate it. It was her own misjudgment that had led to this situation, putting her sister in harm’s way. The continuous reports from the front lines pulled Limestone Pie back from her heavy fantasies. The situation at the front had slightly improved, at least enough to maintain a stalemate with Las Pegasus. If the rock farm could hold out for a few more months, perhaps the greedy Las Pegasus would realize it wasn’t worth the cost, and the tide of the war could turn. But this would mean more innocent ponies being injured or lost during this time. If sacrificing herself could save many families, Limestone Pie wouldn’t hesitate.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_30_o0]
"Limestone Pie, now you don’t have to envy Maud for having her own fiancé."

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_30_o1]
"That’s absurd! There’s no way I’m agreeing to these two freaks！"

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_31]
Rockville Earthquake

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_31_desc]
Today has been a somber day at the rock farm. Without warning, our Rockville region experienced a 6.8 magnitude earthquake, triggering flash floods in the surrounding areas. Many old houses collapsed, and some miners are still trapped deep in the mines awaiting rescue. The local government is formulating rescue plans, while residents are spontaneously helping each other. Nearby areas like Appleloosa have also sent rescue teams to assist us. Some unscrupulous commentators in Las Pegasus mock us, saying that our mining activities are just desserts for us. However, we currently cannot afford to retort to them.As of now, the Equestria Empire has not issued any statement regarding the incident.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_31_o0]
Oh my Godness, may Celestia bless them!

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_32]
The Second Earthquake

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_32_desc]
We must have overlooked something. Right now, scientists from the entire Geological University are scratching their heads, trying to figure out what went wrong. From any perspective, it’s inexplicable and unacceptable to the geologists that just yesterday, Rockville experienced another strong earthquake. Although the magnitude was not as severe as the last one, the violent shaking of the earth once again destroyed the efforts I’ve made over the past few months to rebuild.
Now, more and more ponies believe it’s the radar station that’s causing the problem. Many ponies have gathered in front of the government demanding immediate explanation from the mayor of Rockville. Some radical earth ponies have even picked up shovels from their hooves and are attempting to rush into the radar station to wreak havoc.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_32_o0]
Earthquakes don’t kill ponies — buildings do!

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_33]
Quarray eel

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_33_desc]
As geologists and scientists worked tirelessly day and night, the truth of the matter left all ponies greatly intrigued. It turned out that deep within the Macintosh Mountains lived a vast population of quarray eels. This mysterious carnivorous eel, known and named by geographers for its distribution in the Ghastly Gorge. They lurked in the underground and rock layers, waiting for the opportunity to hunt down unfortunate birds or animals. However, the Macintosh Mountain quarray eels were larger than their other kin. Unlike eels living in the sea, quarray eels usually live on land and underground and can breathe air directly. The Macintosh Mountain quarray eels could even move through rocks.
While some scientists remained curious about this phenomenon, it became apparent that the sensory organs of quarray eels were easily affected by radar waves. When the radar station near Rockville was completed, a large number of quarray eels became restless and collectively migrated, damaging the heavy bedrock beneath Rockville and eventually causing underground collapses and earthquakes. The military expressed strong interest in this, as if we could use the appropriate radio waves, we would have the opportunity to tame these fierce predators and make them fight for our army, launching a fierce attack from unexpected places on the enemy.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_33_o0]
So the radar station was the cause after all

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_34]
Investigation initiation

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_34_desc]
Investigating the source of the earthquakes suddenly became the government’s top priority. Fortunately, our team of geographers had already sprung into action and started preparations. Just as the investigators were unsure where to begin, reports from eyewitnesses of the earthquakes caught their attention. It was said that during the earthquakes, some witnesses were terrified to see creatures emerging from underground, devouring ponies and debris. While the investigators found the eyewitness accounts somewhat unbelievable, the fact remained that some ponies were still missing, although this couldn’t prove anything.

Meanwhile, spurred on by citizens in Rockville, there arose resistance against the radar stations across various regions. This forced us to occasionally shut them down or reduce their power to placate the populace. In order to monitor aerial movements in surrounding areas and avoid being caught off guard, some scientists proposed new designs for radar systems. These designs utilized more sophisticated components, promising increased efficiency and size. With government promotion and subsidies, it should be possible to improve public perception of radar systems.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_34_o0]
Let’s act quickly

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_35]
Another Pinkie Pie

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_35_desc]
Although Maud Pie had repeatedly told herself beforehand that the pony coming through the portal wasn’t her real sister, when she saw the pink figure in the meeting room, uncontrollable tears welled up in the corner of her eyes.
This strange and heartbreaking feeling left Maud Pie feeling puzzled. Throughout her life, Maud Pie had experienced countless hardships and storms, but she had always been able to resolve them firmly and decisively. She had long forgotten how to cry, even when she realized she might never see her most beloved sister again.
But now, her sister — or rather, a pony resembling her sister — was alive and well before her... Maud Pie quickly wiped her eyes with her hoof to prevent the surrounding ponies from seeing. As a core figure at the rock farm, Maud Pie was considered by all harmony-loving ponies to have a will as strong as steel, and she was constantly inspired by her.

After the negotiations with Sunset Shimmer and other leaders of the resistance were over, Maud Pie walked slowly towards the figure who was laughing loudly. She had intended to greet her with a gentle tone, but as she opened her mouth, she found herself unable to speak. When the Pinkie Pie from the mirrored world turned around and saw Maud Pie hesitating in front of her, she tilted her head in confusion:
“Hmm?”

In the midst of the surrounding ponies’ exclamations, Maud Pie hugged her sister tightly, tears streaming down her face.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_35_o0]
“I missed you, sister.”

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_36]
Family reunion

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_36_desc]
At Maud Pie’s invitation, Pinkie Pie from the other world set foot on the land of the rock farm for the first time.
“Oh my goodness, look at these beautiful rocks, and... pebbles! In another world, you have one that looks just like you! ... or maybe it’s her who looks like you? How interesting!”
Maud Pie smiled as she listened to Pinkie Pie’s enthusiasm, silently wishing this moment could last forever.

Meanwhile, Limestone Pie was scolding the guards fiercely. However, when she turned her head and saw that Maud Pie and Pinkie Pie had arrived early, she immediately became flustered and shouted to the guards, “All ponies, a-a-attention!” The guards quickly lined up in two rows, hastily saluting the three ponies.

Some guards almost threw their ceremonial spears into the air, and their comical performance amused Pinkie Pie to no end. As she approached a guard who looked nervous, she playfully tickled his armpit with her hoof, causing him to collapse to the ground in laughter.
Unable to resist any longer, Limestone Pie also embraced Pinkie Pie, pretending to be angry as she said, “Pinkamena Diane Pie, how dare you leave us for so long!”
At that moment, they were not the important leaders of the rock farm or the core of the government department but just the two older sisters of this pink little pony.

A burst of sobbing caught everyone’s attention, and it was the youngest sister of the Pie family, Marble Pie, along with their parents, Igneous Rock and Cloudy Quartz, who were supporting each other. When Marble Pie saw Pinkie Pie, she couldn’t control her tears anymore. Snot and tears messed up her gray mane as Cloudy Quartz approached, pinching Pinkie Pie’s cheeks, hardly believing her eyes.

“Is it really my little Pinkamena?” she asked tremblingly.
“Mom!” Pinkie Pie bounced over to her mother in this world and embraced her tightly.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_36_o0]
“Welcome home, Pinkie Pie!”

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_38]
Another Pinkie Pie

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_38_o0]
“I missed you, sister.”

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_39]
A sudden illness

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_39_desc]
Marble Pie pushed the door open and entered. Limestone Pie was gazing out the window.

"The newly established statistics department reports that last month, the retail price of flour in our farm increased by 0.15% month-on-month and 1.85% year-on-year; apples are retailing at 5.96 bits per kilogram, down 0.17% month-on-month and 1.49% year-on-year... These figures are fascinating! Understanding them isn’t any easier than picking out pyroxenes from hornblende. I've never seen anything like this before. If the princesses were still around, they'd be the ones dealing with these numbers."

Marble Pie giggled. "Perhaps we need to increase grain imports from Las Pegasus. If the opportunity arises, maybe we could even consider doing something to help Starlight Glimmer or Sunset Shimmer..."

Her voice trailed off. She looked up to see Limestone Pie’s solemn face. In the past, Limestone would have likely stroked Marble’s soft cheek and made a playful remark.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_39_o0]
"What’s the matter?"

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_40]
A sudden illness

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_40_desc]
When Marble Pie arrived, she found Igneous Rock and Cloudy Quartz lying unconscious on separate hospital beds. The room was sparsely populated, with her sister Maud Pie and Mudbriar engaged in a tense conversation with a pony dressed as a doctor.

"If you're truly the best doctor the rock farm has," Mudbriar argued, "then you should be able to find a solution." He added curtly, "We can’t let this information leak. The Empire and Las Pegasus would seize any opportunity to exploit this situation."

The doctor responded with concern, "This appears to be a rare, acute illness. Given the current medical facilities on the farm, I'm not optimistic..."

Mudbriar shook his head, interrupting, "I don’t see that as an option. If Igneous Rock and Cloudy Quartz were conscious, they wouldn’t agree to that either."

Maud Pie remained silent, leaning against the bedside. Marble Pie had never seen her sister so sorrowful.

Marble slowly approached and leaned beside Maud. Though she had told herself to stay strong since the Last Roundup, tears streamed down her face uncontrollably. Maud embraced Marble, closed her eyes, and tears fell onto Cloudy Quartz’s hoof.

Cloudy Quartz opened her eyes weakly and said to Marble, "Maudileena... Marble... my sweethearts, I will always love you. It’s time... for your father and me to depart."

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_40_o0]
"I won’t allow it!"

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_41]
action in the shadow

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_41_desc]
Marble Pie stumbled out of the hospital room, her steps unsteady. A wave of dizziness washed over her, and her body still trembled slightly from the sobs that had wracked her moments ago. She brought her forehooves together in a silent plea, yet she didn’t know to whom she was praying. Tears welled up once more, slipping down her cheeks.

Suddenly, she recalled the argument between Mudbriar and the doctor. If what the doctor had said was true, then sacrificing the interests of the rock farm to restore Igneous Rock and Cloudy Quartz to health would be worth it. Moreover, it might provide leverage in negotiations with the Empire. With this thought, Marble Pie nodded shakily. She took a deep breath and sprinted towards the rock farm’s town hall. Her speed and determined expression startled the ponies she passed, who quickly stepped aside.

Upon reaching the telegraph office, she dismissed the other ponies present. Then, she quietly sent a telegram to both the Empire and Las Pegasus.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_41_o0]
Sacrificing everything would be worth it.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_42]
A secret telegram from the rock farm

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_42_desc]
We have just received an urgent telegram from the Rock Farm autonomous territory. Although sent through official channels, the sender remains anonymous. The message reports that the Pie family’s parents—Igneous Rock and Cloudy Quartz—have suddenly fallen into a serious coma, and the Rock Farm lacks medical facilities as advanced as ours. This report has not yet been confirmed, but given the Pie sisters’ world‑renowned filial devotion, such an incident will undoubtedly affect both the Rock Farm and the surrounding region. No further details were provided, but it is clear that, regardless of the sender’s motives, if true, we could leverage our superior medical capabilities to gain political capital over the Rock Farm—an ideal opportunity to assert real control.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_42_o0]
First, dispatch a delegation to verify the facts.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_43]
A sudden illness

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_43_desc]
Maud Pie felt a flutter of apprehension as the Empire’s colossal airship appeared over the rock farm, its shadow sweeping across every pony below. The red banner of the Imperial Empress fluttered atop the vessel, and even those who dared not look up were struck by the Empire’s majesty—and reminded that the rock farm remained merely an autonomous territory. Would Cozy Glow herself pay a personal visit? Why now of all times? Limestone Pie’s thoughts were in turmoil, but there was no time to ponder further: the airship was already descending slowly above the plaza where Holder’s Boulder stood.

A crimson carpet unrolled from the ship’s hatch, and when Dawn Crown and Double Delight swept down its length, the rock farm honor guard on either side presented arms in salute. Maud Pie’s face remained impassive, and the saluting soldiers mirrored her composure—everyone knew it was mere formality, an unspoken understanding. Thankfully, at least the rifles in their hands were loaded only with blanks.

“I thought this was supposed to be a secret visit,” Double Delight murmured to Dawn Crown, a note of awkwardness in her voice.
“Only a show like this will remind these ponies who truly rules them,” Dawn Crown replied, then added softly, “But our mission remains unchanged.”

Double Delight nodded and stepped forward to offer Maud Pie the expected pleasantries. As the welcoming ceremony concluded, the imperial party and their entourage made their way into the rock farm’s private reception hall.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_43_o0]
The negotiations had begun.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_44]
family meeting

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_44_desc]
After all the ponies from the Pie family and the Apple family had taken their seats, Limestone Pie—unlike Maud Pie—didn’t begin by exchanging pleasantries with her sister. Instead, she dove straight into the current state and future prospects of the rock farm. Before long, she shifted the meeting’s focus to military expansion. She detailed the farm’s armaments and what the ponies would need to do if they were to prevail in the next decisive war: longer work hours, broader—and even mandatory—conscription. When she finished speaking, the cramped meeting hall fell deathly silent.

Seats had been left open for Maud Pie and Mudbriar, but Limestone Pie couldn’t yet bring herself to acknowledge their absence. Granite Pie (Igneous Rock) and Cloudy Quartz were similarly missing. Amid the hush, Limestone Pie stared at those empty chairs, lost in thought—until a low voice snapped her back to the present.

“Sister Limestone, I share your grief. Granite Pie and Cloudy Quartz were not only your parents but our kin and family. Blood binds us together. But with all due respect, I can’t support your plan for the future. Every pony at the rock farm deserves the freedom to choose their own path, not be yoked to a war machine for the Empire.”

Limestone Pie looked up, frowning. Who dared speak to her this way? It was Brabon. Her headache deepened as every other Pie and Apple pony in the room silently nodded in agreement with his words.

“I called this meeting today not to argue or negotiate,” Limestone Pie retorted coldly, a note of accusation in her voice. She blamed those who should have stood by her for siding with the Empire despite generations of family enmity. Anger surged, but she drew a deep breath, forcing herself to calm down—she didn’t want to lose her temper in front of those she held dear.

“And if I refuse?” Brabon looked around, then tilted his head, voicing the question on everyone’s mind.

“If you insist on opposing me, then I have no choice but to ask you and your supporters to leave the rock farm,” Limestone Pie declared, placing a hoof on Granite Pie’s empty chair and pointing to the door with her other hoof.

Brabon sighed—he had expected this outcome. He stood first and began to walk out. At the door he paused, turned back, and said, “I understand your pain, and I’m sorry for everything that’s happened… When you’ve had time to think, we will return.” As he stepped outside, the other Apple family delegates and most of the rock‑farm families stood and followed him out of the room.

Limestone Pie slumped in her chair, watching them go. She said nothing to stop them.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_44_o0]
Soon, her eyes changed from sadness to determination and anger

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_45]
family meeting

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_45_desc]
fter all the ponies from the Pie family and the Apple family had taken their seats, Limestone Pie—unlike Maud Pie—didn’t begin by exchanging pleasantries with her sister. Instead, she dove straight into the current state and future prospects of the rock farm. Before long, she shifted the meeting’s focus to military expansion. She detailed the farm’s armaments and what the ponies would need to do if they were to prevail in the next decisive war: longer work hours, broader—and even mandatory—conscription. When she finished speaking, the cramped meeting hall fell deathly silent.

Seats had been left open for Maud Pie and Mudbriar, but Limestone Pie couldn’t yet bring herself to acknowledge their absence. Granite Pie (Igneous Rock) and Cloudy Quartz were similarly missing. Amid the hush, Limestone Pie stared at those empty chairs, lost in thought—until a low voice snapped her back to the present.

“Sister Limestone, I share your grief. Granite Pie and Cloudy Quartz were not only your parents but our kin and family. Blood binds us together. But with all due respect, I can’t support your plan for the future. Every pony at the rock farm deserves the freedom to choose their own path, not be yoked to a war machine for the Empire.”

Limestone Pie looked up, frowning. Who dared speak to her this way? It was Brabon. Her headache deepened as every other Pie and Apple pony in the room silently nodded in agreement with his words.

“I called this meeting today not to argue or negotiate,” Limestone Pie retorted coldly, a note of accusation in her voice. She blamed those who should have stood by her for siding with the Empire despite generations of family enmity. Anger surged, but she drew a deep breath, forcing herself to calm down—she didn’t want to lose her temper in front of those she held dear.

“And if I refuse?” Brabon looked around, then tilted his head, voicing the question on everyone’s mind.

“If you insist on opposing me, then I have no choice but to ask you and your supporters to leave the rock farm,” Limestone Pie declared, placing a hoof on Granite Pie’s empty chair and pointing to the door with her other hoof.

Brabon sighed—he had expected this outcome. He stood first and began to walk out. At the door he paused, turned back, and said, “I understand your pain, and I’m sorry for everything that’s happened… When you’ve had time to think, we will return.” As he stepped outside, the other Apple family delegates and most of the rock‑farm families stood and followed him out of the room.

Inside the hall, Limestone Pie slumped in her chair, watching them go without a single plea for them to stay. Outside the government doors of the quarry domain, Braeburn glanced back to see dozens more kin marching away beside him. Though his heart ached, he found a measure of solace in their solidarity.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_45_o0]
Appleloosa and the Rock Farm separated for a while, but the feelings between the two families are not

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_46]
army coming

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_46_desc]
Limestone Pie wore an impassive expression as she anxiously awaited word from the front—a message that would signify her victory. At her side stood a representative of the Apple family. At this very moment, the thing she valued most since assuming power—her army—was drawn up in perfect formation along the Buffalo Tribe’s border. Her diplomats were locked in fierce verbal sparring with the buffalo, pressing them to throw in their lot with her banner and rejoin the Apple Pie family.

Although the Buffalo Tribe had never been part of the Pie clan, they and the Apples had a long history of feuding over land and resources—conflicts that occasionally erupted into open warfare. Under the two princesses, relations had been softened by the Elements of Harmony, but after the Last Roundup the buffalo chose to break away entirely, retreating to the Buffalo Wastes and ignoring every diplomatic overture from the Apple family. All of Appleloosa’s previous efforts had failed. Yet to Limestone Pie, this very breakdown was an opportunity. She had not forgotten the events at the last family council; now she was determined to prove to Brebron, the Apple family, and the rest of Equestria that she could achieve any aim by force.

Limestone Pie was already planning her next move once the buffalo lands were secured. She felt no hesitation—her orders were clear: should diplomacy falter, her army would march in and seize the territory by force, regardless of the war and its fallout. And then, just as she braced herself,

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_46_o0]
the telegraph finally clicked to life with the eagerly awaited dispatch…

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_47]
the rock farm armies are approaching .

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_47_desc]
Our neighbors at the Rock Farm, who in their recent struggle with the Empire saw the cruel and ruthless Limestone Pie replace her gentle sister Maud Pie, have now firmly thrown off any pretense of kindness. As soon as Limestone Pie took power, she imposed an iron‑fisted rule over the Rock Farm and quickly expanded its army. We have always had no quarrel with the Rock Farm, but, to our disbelief, we have become her very first victims.

Today, disturbing news reached us at our border: the Rock Farm’s forces are massing in great numbers along our frontier—far exceeding the strength of our own border guards. Before long, the Rock Farm’s envoy conveyed Limestone Pie’s hypocritical proposal: she demands that we “lay down our hatred,” end our long‑standing dispute with the Apple family, immediately cease all resistance, and join her alliance with Appleloosa. If we refuse, her army “will be obliged to assist her” in enforcing this outcome.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_47_o0]
We have no choice—at least this way we may still stand as equals afterward.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_47_o1]
Let her bring her full might against us; tell her we will resist to the last.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_48_desc]
Limestone Pie sat back in her chair, closing her eyes and rubbing her face with her hoof to ease her restless anxiety. Why did the Buffalo Tribe, knowing they were outmatched, still refuse to yield? After all, she only wanted to resolve the conflict this way, to prove the worth of her convictions. Did it really have to come to war against the Buffalo Tribe, even though it would inevitably cost countless lives and leave so many displaced?

“sister Limestone , this isn’t who you really are. If you do this, how are you any different from that tyrant in Canterlot?” the Appleloosa envoy murmured.

“Shut up! You don’t get to make decisions here!” Limestone Pie couldn’t contain her anger and bellowed at the poor mare. Almost immediately, she regretted her harsh tone—it was uncalled for. But the arrow had been loosed: her forces were waiting on the front line for her final orders. If she didn’t subdue the Buffalo Tribe quickly, they wouldn’t secure the local mineral fields, nor could they launch a surprise attack on the Empire from around Cherry Hill.

After a moment’s reflection, Limestone Pie softened. She offered the mare a gentle apology and said:

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_48_o0]
To defeat the Empire, the Buffalo Tribe has left me no choice. it’s their own fault.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_48_o1]
I never wanted to become an executioner like Cozy Glow… ”

[en.PIHC_C12_STOP_WAR_ON_BUFFALO_TOOLTIP]
Stop the war on buffalo

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_49]
Limestone Pie’s Claim on the Buffalo Tribe

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_49_desc]
Since the last family council, Limestone Pie has been feverishly expanding her forces and preparing for war. Determined to defeat the Empire outright on the battlefield, she is willing to pay any price—even if it means sacrificing us.

Recently, our Apple family envoy at the rock farm sent us a terrifying dispatch: in order to test her armed strength and to open a second front against the Empire, Limestone Pie has decided to turn her attention to the Buffalo Tribe—long-standing rivals of ours—and force them into total subjugation. Although we and the Buffalo Tribe have frequently clashed, we have never lost our reason as Limestone Pie has.

Everypony knows that if Limestone Pie succeeds this time in imposing her will, she is highly likely to repeat the same tactic again—until one day it may be used against us, should we stand in her way.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_49_o0]
Dispatch another family member to persuade Limestone Pie to abandon this course of action.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_50_desc]
Limestone Pie received the latest word from the front: the Buffalo Tribe had refused to submit and was prepared to fight to the death. She sat back in her chair, closed her eyes, and rubbed her face with her hoof to ease her anxiety. She couldn’t understand why the Buffalo, knowing they were outmatched, refused to yield—especially when all she’d wanted was to resolve the conflict on her own terms and prove her convictions. Did she really have to go to war against them, even if it meant countless casualties and leaving scores of buffalo displaced?

“Sister Limestone , this isn’t the real you. If you go through with this, how are you any different from that fellow in Canterlot?” the Appleloosa envoy whispered.

“Shut up! You have no say in this!” Limestone Pie could not contain her anger and snapped at the poor filly. Almost immediately, regret welled up—she shouldn’t have been so harsh. But there was no turning back now: her army awaiting her final orders at the front could not be held in check. If she did not subdue the Buffalo Tribe swiftly, she would lose any claim on the local minerals and forego the chance to launch an unexpected strike on the Empire from Cherry Hills.

After a moment’s thought, Limestone Pie softened. She offered the filly a gentle apology and then spoke with firm resolve:
“To defeat the Empire, the Buffalo left me no choice—it’s their own fault.”

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_50_o0]
Limestone Pie’s eyes were utterly lost to hatred

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_51_desc]
Limestone Pie received the latest word from the front: the Buffalo Tribe had refused to submit and was prepared to fight to the death. She sat back in her chair, closed her eyes, and rubbed her face with her hoof to ease her anxiety. She couldn’t understand why the Buffalo, knowing they were outmatched, refused to yield—especially when all she’d wanted was to resolve the conflict on her own terms and prove her convictions. Did she really have to go to war against them, even if it meant countless casualties and leaving scores of buffalo displaced?

“Sister Limestone , this isn’t the real you. If you go through with this, how are you any different from that fellow in Canterlot?” the Appleloosa envoy whispered.

“Shut up! You have no say in this!” Limestone Pie could not contain her anger and snapped at the poor filly. Almost immediately, regret welled up—she shouldn’t have been so harsh. But there was no turning back now: her army awaiting her final orders at the front could not be held in check. If she did not subdue the Buffalo Tribe swiftly, she would lose any claim on the local minerals and forego the chance to launch an unexpected strike on the Empire from Cherry Hills.

After a moment’s thought, Limestone Pie softened. She offered the filly a gentle apology and then spoke with firm resolve:
“I’m sorry, I’ve been feeling out of sorts lately… I don’t actually want to be an executioner like Cozy Glow.”Then, she issued the order to withdraw the troops from the front line.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_51_o0]
There is still a shred of rationality in her heart

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_52_desc]
Our border guards have brought us troubling news: large columns of troops and engineering vehicles from the rock farm are rapidly massing in the direction of Breezies Village. A similar tactic was used before against the Buffalo Tribe—Limestone Pie, under the guise of “resolving family disputes,” forcibly conquered them and hailed it as her great victory. Now, simply because the land of Breezies Village holds valuable resources, an assault by Limestone Pie seems all but certain.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_52_o0]
We have no choice but to fall back.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_52_o1]
Breezies Village? Not on our watch!

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_52_TENSION]
Breezies Invaded

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_53]
The Displaced Breezies

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_53_desc]
Seabreeze was carefully placed into a clear glass jar by an enlisted officer and gently set inside an exquisitely crafted box. She offered no resistance, for she knew it would be futile. Just moments ago, the same fate had befallen every Breezie: troop after troop of soldiers dismounted from their chariots—this officer among them—and without warning crammed the Breezies into separate jars. Although the soldiers tried not to injure them, their actions still provoked panic, and chaos ensued. The Breezies’ tiny town was trampled and demolished in the confusion. One soldier grabbed a megaphone to restore order and blared assurances of safety, but the blast only forced the Breezies to cover their ears and writhe in pain.

Yet when Seabreeze saw the hesitancy and darting eyes of the officer before her, she summoned all her strength and pounded the glass jar, producing dull thuds. But the jar remained unmoved. Born of wind magic, she could stir air itself—but she couldn’t even topple this glass prison.

“What did we ever do wrong? Why are you treating us like this? I thought… I thought we were friends,” she sobbed, her tears blurring her vision as she cried out at the top of her voice. The officer sighed and turned away, unable to meet her gaze. “Limestone Pie has arranged a safer place for you,” he offered weakly. “There you won’t be harmed again.”

“Let me see Limestone Pie! This has been our home for generations—a thousand years, and the only ones who’ve truly hurt us are you!” Seabreeze’s voice quivered with righteous anger. “You’ve destroyed this beautiful land, built fortresses here, blasted open quarries, driven out its creatures, and turned it into a battlefield…” Each accusation rang in the officer’s heart, yet his small frame and uniform rendered him powerless to answer.

With a final sigh, the officer snapped the box shut,

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_53_o0]
and Seabreeze’s cries faded into a trembling silence.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_54]
Private Consultation

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_54_desc]
Marble Pie stood anxiously pacing before the private office of the Flim Flam brothers. The two guards flanking the door stared at her without blinking, making her feel deeply uncomfortable. With a creak, the ornate door was pulled open, and Marble Pie hurried inside. As soon as she stepped in, the door swung shut behind her with a slow, groaning creak. There was no butler pony waiting, nor any glimmer of magic—an oddity that piqued Marble’s curiosity. But when she saw the two brothers smiling at her, her nerves returned and she swallowed hard before hurrying to sit in the chair in front of them.

For a moment, both brothers sat in complete silence, watching her intently, much like the guards had. At last, a timid voice escaped from the fillies lips: “U-um… today… I’m here… on behalf of the Rock Farm…” Marble Pie tried to speak, but found it much harder than she’d anticipated.

“Oh, my dear Marble Pie, no need to be so nervous,” Flim said, reclining further in his chair and interlacing his forehooves behind his head in a relaxed gesture. “Why don’t we start by discussing why your lovely sister didn’t come herself—why send you instead?”

“Ah… well… Sister said… I’m easier to talk to… and you’d like me better…” Marble Pie stammered.

“Ho ho ho, is that so?” Flam laughed, bounding up to Marble’s side and leaning in close, as if teasing her. “Well then… what exactly does your sister wish to say to us? Could it be… a proposal of sorts? To me, Flam? Or perhaps to both of us?”

“No, no, nothing like that!” Marble Pie blushed deeply and shook her head.

Finally gathering her courage, she cleared her throat and said quietly,

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_54_o0]
"She hopes to negotiate a non‑aggression pact with Las Pegasus"

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_55]
condtion of the brothers

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_55_desc]
Upon hearing this, Flim’s ears perked up instantly. "Oh?"

Marble Pie quickly added, "She also said that as long as the request isn’t too excessive, she can fulfill it." As she spoke, she buried her head in her mane, leaving only her big eyes peeking out to observe the brothers’ reactions.

Flim hesitated for a moment, then looked up and exchanged a glance with Flam at the other end of the table. They immediately understood each other.

"Oh dear, my Marble Pie, you have such audacity. Betraying that young alicorn comes with a hefty price," Flim exclaimed.

"Indeed, indeed. I shall inform Her Majesty Cozy Glow right away and accuse your Pie family of attempted treason. Guards, where are the guards?" Flam shouted in succession.

The brothers took turns shouting. At some point, Flim pulled out a handkerchief from his pocket, pressed it to his forehead, closed his eyes, and fell backward. Flam jumped from the table to catch his brother steadily, performing a drama in front of Marble Pie.

"Ooh," Marble Pie, seeing that the brothers had no intention of agreeing, became anxious. Tears welled up in her eyes. "Please, don’t do this... Even if... you set a condition, I'll agree to it!"

This was exactly what the brothers wanted to hear. They exchanged a smile, and Flim leaned close to Marble Pie’s face and said, "Really? Any condition?"

Marble Pie immediately nodded her head like a bobblehead.

"Then our condition is..." Flam stood tall atop the table, gazing ahead with shining eyes, raising his hoof as if solemnly swearing. Then, the two brothers said in unison:

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_56_desc]
Marble Pie stood anxiously pacing before the private office of the Flim Flam brothers. The two guards flanking the door stared at her without blinking, making her feel deeply uncomfortable. With a creak, the ornate door was pulled open, and Marble Pie hurried inside. As soon as she stepped in, the door swung shut behind her with a slow, groaning creak. There was no butler pony waiting, nor any glimmer of magic—an oddity that piqued Marble’s curiosity. But when she saw the two brothers smiling at her, her nerves returned and she swallowed hard before hurrying to sit in the chair in front of them.

For a moment, both brothers sat in complete silence, watching her intently, much like the guards had. At last, a timid voice escaped from the fillies lips: “U-um… today… I’m here… on behalf of the Rock Farm…” Marble Pie tried to speak, but found it much harder than she’d anticipated.

“Oh, my dear Marble Pie, no need to be so nervous,” Flim said, reclining further in his chair and interlacing his forehooves behind his head in a relaxed gesture. “Why don’t we start by discussing why your lovely sister didn’t come herself—why send you instead?”

“Ah… well… Sister said… I’m easier to talk to… but I'm... I'm not here to surrender!” Marble Pie stammered.

“Ho ho ho, so?” Flam laughed, bounding up to Marble’s side and leaning in close, as if teasing her. “Well then… what exactly does your sister wish to say to us? Could it be… a proposal of sorts? To me, Flam? Or perhaps to both of us?”

“No, no, nothing like that!” Marble Pie blushed deeply and shook her head.

Finally gathering her courage, she cleared her throat and said quietly,

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_56_o0]
"She hopes to negotiate a non‑aggression pact with Las Pegasus"

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_57]
condtion of the brothers

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_57_desc]
Upon hearing this, Flim’s ears perked up instantly. "Oh?"

Marble Pie quickly added, "She also said that as long as the request isn’t too excessive, she can fulfill it." As she spoke, she buried her head in her mane, leaving only her big eyes peeking out to observe the brothers’ reactions.

Flim hesitated for a moment, then looked up and exchanged a glance with Flam at the other end of the table. They immediately understood each other.

"Oh dear, my Marble Pie, you have such audacity. Betraying that young alicorn comes with a hefty price," Flim exclaimed.

"Indeed, indeed. I shall inform Her Majesty Cozy Glow right away and accuse your Pie family of attempted treason.""Yes, yes! Guards! Seize this traitor to the Empress!" Flam shouted in succession.

The brothers took turns shouting. At some point, Flim pulled out a handkerchief from his pocket, pressed it to his forehead, closed his eyes, and fell backward. Flam jumped from the table to catch his brother steadily, performing a drama in front of Marble Pie.

"Ooh," Marble Pie, seeing that the brothers had no intention of agreeing, became anxious. Tears welled up in her eyes. "Please, don’t do this... Even if... you set a condition, I'll agree to it!"

This was exactly what the brothers wanted to hear. They exchanged a smile, and Flim leaned close to Marble Pie’s face and said, "Really? Any condition?"

Marble Pie immediately nodded her head like a bobblehead.

"Then our condition is..." Flam stood tall atop the table, gazing ahead with shining eyes, raising his hoof as if solemnly swearing. Then, the two brothers said in unison:

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_58]
first test

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_58_desc]
A few months ago, during a routine high-level meeting at the rock farm, Limestone Pie presented a set of blueprints left behind by Pinkie Pie. Pinkie had envisioned a suit of earth pony armor—or rather, a miniature weapons platform—that was not only robust enough to withstand most light weaponry but also equipped with the firepower of an entire squad, all mounted on a single platform. This design promised both mobility and formidable strength.

However, while the concept was promising, its implementation posed significant challenges. Simply mounting weapons and armor onto an earth pony without modifications would be overwhelming, potentially crushing the wearer under the weight.

In the ensuing months, the research team assembled the best experts available at the rock farm to initiate the project and commence rigorous testing. Today marked the first official trial. Limestone Pie, Banana Mash, and Platinum Cure were among those present to observe.

Upon arriving at the testing grounds, a remarkably sturdy earth pony saluted Limestone Pie. Banana Mash explained, "This pony is an elite selected from our active forces, possessing one of the most robust physiques in the army. Now, please give the order."

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_58_o0]
Limestone Pie then commanded the test to commence.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_59]
Experimental result

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_59_desc]
The tester stood at the center of the testing platform, beaming with excitement. Nearby, the lab ponies diligently attached armor and weapons to him. However, when the final piece of armor was secured, the entire team erupted in cheers and hoof stomps. Yet, Limestone Pie’s face remained devoid of a smile. She noticed that the tester’s expression had become increasingly uncomfortable. One of the lab ponies asked, "Shall we try taking a couple of steps forward?" Gritting his teeth, the tester took a step. The pistons in his joints began to grind, emitting a series of sounds. Unfortunately, the scene that all present hoped to avoid occurred. With a sharp crack from the tester’s body, his eyes glazed over, and he collapsed heavily to the ground. Some armor components loosened and fell off. The experiment had failed, and cheers turned into gasps. Several lab ponies quickly rushed over to assist him. Limestone Pie’s expression darkened as she shook her head.

"It seems that with our current technology, we can’t fully equip a pony with all this heavy weaponry," lamented banana mash. As a researcher handed her the report, she sighed and said, "It seems we're far from it. Though it’s unfortunate, I believe this approach is unworkable. We can’t balance firepower and portability. These weapons should truly be mounted on vehicles and tanks, not on a single earth pony."

platinum cure, while reviewing the report, furrowed his brow without hastening to offer an opinion. "platinum cure, what do you think?" Limestone Pie asked, testing the waters, though she held little hope. "Simply modifying the weapons and attempting to equip a single pony with them isn’t feasible. Even the best research teams in all of Equestria can’t achieve this," he replied. After a pause, he shifted his tone. "Unless... are you familiar with potionology? In my youth, I dabbled in this field on Zebra Island. If we take a different approach and infuse a specific potion formula into an earth pony, we might enhance their physique, significantly increasing their carrying capacity." Just as Limestone Pie was about to speak, platinum cure added, "However, you must understand that such biological modifications have historically been prohibited due to their high mortality rates and other potential risks. Moreover, if we aim to create a sufficiently large army, many ponies might perish. I cannot guarantee the safety of any of them. Before you make a decision, I must remind you of this."

Limestone Pie hesitated. Her mouth opened and closed as she gazed at the collapsed earth pony and the bustling lab ponies. After a moment of contemplation, she responded:

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_59_o0]
"Proceed with it. The lives of ordinary ponies are inconsequential."

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_59_o1]
"Alternatively, as banana mash suggested, we could consider vehicle platforms."

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_60_desc]
When the carefully selected Earth pony soldier appeared before Limestone Pie, her eyes lit up, and a long-lost smile graced her face. At that moment, platinum cure stood nearby, explaining the significant achievements he had made in potionology over the past few months and the number of fearless Earth ponies who had sacrificed their lives. However, Limestone Pie paid no attention to these details, for this soldier embodied much of the hope to defeat the Empire and any formidable enemy. Before platinum cure could finish his speech, Limestone Pie promptly interrupted him, saying, "We can discuss these matters later. Now, let the experiment begin."

platinum cure wisely fell silent. As the command was given, the Earth pony stood motionless at the center of the experimental platform, just as he had months ago. The research ponies equipped him with weapons and armor. Over the past few months, there had been breakthroughs in weapon integration, successfully reducing weight without compromising firepower. Once the final installation was complete, the soldier remained composed.

"Take a few steps forward to test it," came the command, just as before. The soldier first took a few steps forward, then broke into a swift run, circling the area. Next, he aimed at the designated target and fired, demonstrating astonishing combat prowess. The experimental team present finally broke into smiles—the experiment was a success.

Limestone Pie then instructed the team to standardize the process as soon as possible to establish an armed force and, at any cost, recruit qualified participants throughout the entire army.

That night, Limestone Pie tossed and turned, unable to sleep. A legion dedicated solely to her would soon appear on any battlefield, delivering the most devastating blows to the enemy. However, a deeper desire began to emerge in her mind.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_60_o0]
The end of the Empire was approaching.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_61]
Office Encounter

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_61_desc]
Since the Bison Incident, the relationship between the Apple family and the Pie family has been further strained following the failed family meeting. Both families are aware that their bond is becoming increasingly fragile. Previously unused border outposts are now being reactivated, and Apple family soldiers are appearing along the long-forgotten borders.

Recalling the family meeting from a few months ago, Limestone Pie still feels a surge of anger. She never expected the Apple family and Braeburn to be so heartless, lacking any sense of the bigger picture. Pouring herself a glass of apple cider, she gazes at the strategic map before her, lost in thought. She doesn’t realize her eyes have narrowed slightly until she hears a voice from behind—

“Yo, cousin, what are you thinking about?”

It’s her annoying cousin, Octavio Pie. As one of the few stallions in the Pie family, he always acts arrogantly and never shows her any respect.

“Octavio, I'm not in the mood to deal with your nonsense right now.”

Limestone Pie responds curtly. At this moment, she really wants to go back to the past and complain to Grandma Pie, hoping she wouldn’t spoil this troublesome guy so much.

“What’s wrong? Still thinking about Appleloosa and the Apple family?”

Octavio continues, humming a tune as he approaches. Limestone Pie takes another sip of apple cider without replying.

“I was sitting next to Peach Cream at the time. She actually agreed with your point at first.”

Octavio continues. “Until Braeburn stood up and stirred things up, everything went south.”

Limestone Pie’s eyes widen. Octavio’s words aren’t necessarily wrong. She turns her head and asks,

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_61_o0]
“What do you mean by that?”

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_62]
Office Encounter

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_62_desc]
Octavio shrugged. "I saw you sulking here, so I thought I'd say something to comfort you. Think about it—how could every pony in the Apple family oppose you? The Apple family has always had a strained relationship with the buffalo. Besides, you're doing this to increase our chances of defeating the Empire. Anyway, I'm supporting you."

"If you were the leader of the Pie family, I don’t think we'd have so many problems..."

"That’s enough," interrupted Limestone Pie. "Go back to your Air Force headquarters and stop bothering me."

Octavio muttered something, made a face at her, and slowly left. The room was once again empty, save for Limestone Pie standing alone.

Limestone Pie gazed at the map, her eyes fixed on Appleloosa. A chilling thought began to form in her mind:

"If there’s a way to temporarily 'remove' Braeburn from the Apple family—even if it’s just for a few months—I could use this opportunity to take control of both branches of the Apple family. While Appleloosa hasn’t completely severed ties with the rock farm, I must act quickly. If I wait too long, this opportunity may never come again."

Realizing her own thoughts, Limestone Pie shuddered involuntarily. She quickly shook her head, trying to dispel the idea, but it lingered.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_62_o0]
"Send an agent to knock Braeburn out for a while, just enough for me to take over the Apple family. It'll be fine."

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_62_o1]
"I can’t do that. He’s my relative."

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_63]
Covert Operation

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_63_desc]
Mossy Scent picked up the two packets of powder, her heart pounding. She hadn’t caught a single word from Octavio Pie, the Air Marshal of the rock farm, who stood before her. Tomorrow, she would return to Appleloosa, and as Braeburn’s secretary, she was to introduce this special powder into his teacup. According to the prior agreement, the powder would gradually render him unconscious for one to two weeks, providing Limestone Pie the opportunity to seize leadership of the Apple family amidst their internal turmoil.

Mossy Scent had always admired her sister, Limestone Pie. In her younger years, she had never heard of the Pie family or the rock farm. It wasn’t until a few years ago, with the help of Applejack and Pinkie Pie, that the two families reconnected, and she naturally came to know Limestone. To her, although Limestone often appeared stern, she always had everyone’s best interests at heart.

"Did you understand?" Octavio gave Mossy Scent a slight shake, startling her.

"I understand what needs to be done," Mossy Scent nodded, then pulled up her cloak and quickly left the place, ensuring no other pony noticed her.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_63_o0]
The next day, she took the earliest train back to Appleloosa.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_64]
In Braeburn’s office

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_64_desc]
"Mossy Scent, my dear sister, welcome back. Did your trip to the rock farm yield any fruitful results?" Braeburn gently patted her head, smiling warmly. The gesture startled Mossy Scent, but she quickly composed herself. Of course, she knew Braeburn was likely unaware of her personal matters. After all, she had officially visited the rock farm to discuss economic policies. Surely, no other pony knew about her situation with Octavio... right?

"Yes... the Pie family was as hospitable as ever," Mossy Scent nodded, responding calmly.

Upon hearing the mention of the Pie family, Braeburn sighed and turned to gaze out the window. "Did you see Limestone Pie? Did she mention what she’s been up to lately?"

Mossy Scent quietly stepped closer to Braeburn’s desk, her hoof slipping into her pocket, fingers brushing against the packet of powder. Her heart began to race, but she kept her voice steady and sweet: "She said she hopes our two families can return to the harmonious times of the past."

"Really? She truly feels that way?" Braeburn turned sharply toward Mossy Scent, making her hold her breath, then looked back out the window. "Actually... I have always understood her. She is still waiting for her family's Pinkie Pie to return, just as I am still waiting for our Applejack. Three years, and the Empire has never given us one credible answer. I share her hatred for that cursed Empress." He slammed a hoof against the wall. "But she has lost all patience and become blinded. I cannot watch our two families be led into an abyss of hatred."

As Braeburn continued to speak his heartfelt thoughts, Mossy Scent hesitated. She had never realized that Braeburn also fervently wished to overthrow the empire. Reflecting on his words, she pondered whether their actions might only darken the future of both families. A sense of unease settled over her, realizing that the fate of their families rested in her hooves.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_64_o0]
Mossy Scent returned the powder to her pocket, abandoning the thought.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_65]
Braeburn’s Funeral

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_65_desc]
As Braeburn lay quietly in his casket, the surrounding Apple family ponies were engulfed in profound despair. Applejack, Big McIntosh, Sugar Belle, and even Apple Bloom—now it was Braeburn’s turn. Over the years, the Apple family had endured far too many unexpected tragedies and hardships. Limestone Pie and other members of the Pie family were also invited to the funeral. However, to everyone’s surprise, while all the ponies wore deep black attire, Limestone Pie chose to don a military uniform. Yet, this action did not meet with much opposition from most ponies.

As Braeburn’s closest siblings tearfully recounted their memories of him, and after receiving a signal from a few Apple family members, Limestone Pie stepped forward to deliver a speech:

"All the ponies of the Apple and Pie families know that in the past, Braeburn and I had deep disagreements. He accused me of being consumed by a desire for vengeance for our family, saying that I was driven by hatred and couldn’t see the right path forward. Since our families’ meetings, he had been stirring up opposition between the two clans. However, I want to say that I don’t blame him at all. There was some truth in his words. He hoped that the Apple family could continue to blossom and bear fruit in this chaotic era, like an apple tree in a storm. But I also know that deep down, he supported my previous actions..."

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_65_o0]
The Apple family ponies present began to stir, but Limestone Pie continued her speech.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_66]
Braeburn’s Funeral

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_66_desc]
Limestone Pie stood with tears in her eyes, her voice rising to a fervent pitch that made every Apple family pony present tremble:

    "But you never know—what comes first: the Empire or tomorrow?

    We all know now there’s evidence that Braeburn’s death was the work of Imperial agents. Simply because the Empress saw him as too influential within the Apple family, she seized the opportunity to have him eliminated. She kicked at our apple tree with all her might, hoping to snap the entire Apple family in half, to throw us into chaos, to rob us of the courage to resist her.

    But I ask you—will you choose to lose your courage? Or will you show her your fury? Will you make her regret, for the rest of her miserable life, ever making enemies of the Apple and Pie families?

    Think of Braeburn and Big McIntosh, dead by the Empire's hoof, and then of Applejack, whose truth the Empire still conceals. The Apple family has had enough. Think of Igneous Rock and Cloudy Quartz, and then of Pinkie Pie, from whom no word has come since she disappeared. The Pie family has had enough. If our two families join hooves once more, we can crush the Empire beneath them and make it pay for the dead, the missing, and every future it stole."

As she finished, many Apple family ponies had already risen to their hooves. One shouted, "Long live the Apple family! Long live the Pie family!" The solemn atmosphere of the funeral gave way to a chorus of impassioned voices and stomping hooves.

Limestone Pie glanced at Braeburn’s peaceful form and felt a pang of guilt. Perhaps, when she one day stands atop the castle in Canterlot, Braeburn’s spirit will forgive her for what she has done.

She scanned the eyes of every pony present. Good. They burned with the same righteous anger as hers. Perhaps the Empress would soon learn of this speech. Perhaps she already had. But it didn’t matter—because the hour of final vengeance was drawing near.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_66_o0]
Limestone Pie’s purpose had been fulfilled. The Apple family had set hoof on the path she had envisioned.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_67]
A Spectacular Failure

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_67_desc]
In a secluded meeting room, Limestone Pie watched the heated argument before her with growing irritation. Before her, Octavio and Mossy were engaged in a fiery exchange, their faces flushed with anger.

"You mean to say you poured both packets of powder in? I told you—did you not listen to a single word? You've killed him! How could the Apple family have someone as foolish as you?"

"That’s nonsense! You... you never mentioned anything about two packets! You just told me to pour the powder in when he wasn’t looking."

"If it were that simple, why would I have packaged them separately..."

"Enough!" Limestone Pie’s voice cut through the room. The two ponies fell silent, their expressions turning anxious as they awaited their sister’s judgment, as if she were a fair judge and they the defendant and plaintiff.

However, Limestone Pie was no longer concerned with assigning blame. Right and wrong had lost their significance. Half an hour ago, she had received news of Braeburn’s death—poisoning was the cause. The Apple family had invited the Pie family to attend the funeral, unaware that Mossy was responsible. They had conveniently attributed the incident to the Empire. Although this outcome far exceeded Limestone Pie’s initial expectations, the current situation seemed to be unfolding in her favor. Given the Apple family’s longstanding resentment towards the Empire, she no longer needed to contemplate how to assume leadership of the Apple family.

"Braeburn’s death is now a settled matter. I don’t care what transpired at the time, but you must not let a single word slip. Otherwise, all our efforts will have been in vain."

She then turned to comfort Mossy, saying, "I know Braeburn’s death was our doing, but don’t blame yourself too much. After all, it was my idea." Upon hearing this, Mossy lowered her head and wiped away tears with her hoof. Octavio also ceased his muttering, remaining silent.

After a moment, Limestone Pie continued,

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_67_o0]
"Now, we have a funeral to attend."

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_68]
Failed Secret Operation

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_68_desc]
"Do you know how long I've been preparing for this? You idiot! In my opinion, you just didn’t have the guts," Limestone Pie watched the heated argument before her with growing irritation. Although, in theory, she should have been the angriest, she simply wasn’t in the mood.

When Mossy returned to the secret meeting room, the disappointing outcome that Limestone Pie and Octavio had feared came to pass: despite her efforts, Mossy hadn’t found the opportunity to carry out the plan. Braeburn was still alive and well. Octavio, unable to contain his frustration, began hurling insults, leading to a shouting match between the two. Yet, Limestone Pie sensed there might be more to the story.

Fortunately, Braeburn hadn’t detected Limestone Pie’s intentions. Otherwise, the situation could have escalated, allowing Cozy Glow to benefit from the chaos. As it stood, things were unfortunate but not disastrous.

"Enough! Both of you, be quiet!" Limestone Pie commanded. The two ponies fell silent. Mossy felt a pang of guilt. She had, in fact, had a chance but couldn’t bring herself to go through with it.

"Mossy, I don’t blame you. Don’t beat yourself up over this," Limestone Pie said. Mossy looked at her sister with gratitude. Seeing Limestone Pie’s stance, Octavio scoffed dismissively.

Limestone Pie didn’t dwell on the matter. In the face of reality, right and wrong seemed irrelevant. What truly mattered was determining the next course of action. She had been so close to bringing all of Appleloosa under her control. She wasn’t ready to accept defeat and let all her efforts go to waste.

Observing Limestone Pie deep in thought, Octavio sensed her resolve and, with a mix of curiosity and apprehension, asked, "You're not thinking of giving up, are you?" Limestone Pie didn’t respond. She simply gestured for the two to leave.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_68_o0]
Limestone Pie decides to continue planning a military coup to overthrow Braeburn.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_68_o1]
Limestone Pie ultimately abandons her dangerous idea.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_69]
Braeburn’s Funeral

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_69_desc]
Limestone Pie stood with tears in her eyes, her voice rising to a fervent pitch that made every Apple family pony present tremble:

    "But you never know—what comes first: the Empire or tomorrow?

    We all know now there’s evidence that Braeburn’s death was the work of Imperial agents. Simply because the Empress saw him as too influential within the Apple family, she seized the opportunity to have him eliminated. She kicked at our apple tree with all her might, hoping to snap the entire Apple family in half, to throw us into chaos, to rob us of the courage to resist her.

    But I ask you—will you choose to lose your courage? Or will you show her your fury? Will you make her regret, for the rest of her miserable life, ever making enemies of the Apple and Pie families?

    Think of Braeburn and Big McIntosh, dead by the Empire's hoof, and then of Applejack, whose truth the Empire still conceals. The Apple family has had enough. Think of Igneous Rock and Cloudy Quartz, and then of Pinkie Pie, from whom no word has come since she disappeared. The Pie family has had enough. If our two families join hooves once more, we can crush the Empire beneath them and make it pay for the dead, the missing, and every future it stole."

As she finished, many Apple family ponies had already risen to their hooves. One shouted, "Long live the Apple family! Long live the Pie family!" The solemn atmosphere of the funeral gave way to a chorus of impassioned voices and stomping hooves.

Limestone Pie glanced at Braeburn’s peaceful form and felt a pang of guilt. Perhaps, when she one day stands atop the castle in Canterlot, Braeburn’s spirit will forgive her for what she has done.

She scanned the eyes of every pony present. Good. They burned with the same righteous anger as hers. Perhaps the Empress would soon learn of this speech. Perhaps she already had. But it didn’t matter—because the hour of final vengeance was drawing near.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_69_o0]
Limestone Pie’s purpose had been fulfilled. The Apple family had set hoof on the path she had envisioned.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_70]
Advancing into Appleloosa

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_70_desc]
When the border guards of the rock farm received orders from their superiors to enter Appleloosa, none of the ponies could hide their confusion. However, their duty was to obey. The Appleloosa ponies watched in astonishment as columns of soldiers, bearing the banners of Limestone Pie and the rock farm, marched past them.

Some patrols from Appleloosa’s own forces soon engaged in skirmishes with the rock farm troops. Yet, many more chose silence and inaction, having received no directives from their higher-ups. Throughout the operation, no significant resistance was encountered.

Hours earlier, following Limestone Pie’s instructions, the pro-war faction within the Apple family acted swiftly. Armed, they detained Braeburn and several other relatives. The operation proceeded without bloodshed. Insider reports suggest that Braeburn had opportunities to order a counterattack or escape but refrained, unwilling to oppose his kin.

Notably, Appleloosa’s military remained uninvolved in the coup, as many of its senior officers were orchestrators of the takeover.

Upon confirmation of the successful coup, Limestone Pie and her forces entered Appleloosa triumphantly, proclaiming the reunion of the Pie and Apple families and committing to a campaign of "blood for blood."

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_70_o0]
Limestone Pie’s objectives were achieved; the Apple family embarked on the path she had envisioned.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_71]
Furious Outburst

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_71_desc]
"Are you telling me that Limestone Pie not only unified Appleloosa overnight but is also clamoring for vengeance on behalf of the Apple family? And the target of her revenge is me? She’s accusing me of murdering Braeburn?" Cozy Glow could hardly believe her ears upon hearing the news. A torrent of questions flooded her mind, surpassing even the day’s administrative tasks. "Are you serious? What does this have to do with me!" She fumed, leaping up and down on her throne. However, she soon regained her composure and continued:

"Why haven’t I heard anything about her before?" She then flew over to another imperial official, who was trembling on the ground. "And you! Didn’t you frequently report to me, saying that she not only voluntarily increased taxes but also expressed unconditional support for me? Otherwise, I would have planned to suppress those troublemakers long ago." The imperial official quivered and replied, "Your Majesty, everything I said was true. It’s just that Limestone Pie presents one face publicly and another in private. We... we've all been deceived by her."

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_71_o0]
"Damn it!"

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_72]
The Trial of Death

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_72_desc]
“Although the infusion process and formula have been revised dozens of times since the initial successful experiment, I must still strongly warn you: the mortality rate of subjects remains close to 50%, and 86.5% of them experience psychological or physical side effects after transformation. I really don’t recommend this. You might not survive, and even if you do, the outcome may not be as pleasant as you imagine.” Platinum Cure said seriously to Limestone Pie.

At this moment, Limestone Pie stood naked, entering a precision glass chamber. The chamber was connected to various tangled pipelines and equipment, many of which emitted red light and released thick steam. The entire room was drowned out by the roar of engines. However, Platinum Cure’s words were unusually clear.

“Big sister!” Limestone Pie’s younger sister, Marble Pie, stood beside Platinum Cure, her voice trembling with worry. She was truly concerned; if she lost Limestone Pie, she would be left all alone. The thought of a failed experiment made her shiver uncontrollably.

“Don’t cry, Marble Pie. If I die, the rock farm will be entrusted to you. If you need help, go find Cheese Sandwich.” Limestone Pie spoke calmly, closing the hatch with her hoof.
Reverso Context

However, she was the one with the most burning anger among the ponies present. Cozy Glow, Tirek, Windigo, and Queen Chrysalis—all possessed extraordinary powers. Limestone Pie was eager to witness their deaths firsthand. But for an ordinary earth pony mare, this was still too challenging. Cozy Glow could shatter her entire body with a single strike. But now, she had the opportunity to change this reality.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_72_o0]
The trial for Limestone Pie had begun.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_73]
Anger and Fire

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_73_desc]
When Limestone Pie closed the hatch, Platinum Cure remained silent, merely gesturing for the other ponies to start the machinery. He had tried to persuade her countless times before, but she had changed; she was seldom willing to listen to others anymore. A torrent of boiling potion began to pour into the chamber, and Limestone felt as if her entire body were being seared by fire. She was submerged in the magical brew, unable to breathe, each drop attempting to tear through her skin and enter her body. The excruciating pain nearly caused her to lose consciousness. In her dazed state, she once again saw Fire Rock and Mica, as well as her sister.

"Perhaps this is my end," she thought, her mind clouded, and she closed her eyes.

However, she then saw the rock farm and Canterlot burning in flames. She seemed to hear once more the nauseating tone of that Empress, the voice growing nearer, whispering in her ear, "If you're going to die, then I want you to be buried with me."

Without hesitation, Limestone extended her hoof and swung it toward the source of the voice. Before she could trample Cozy Glow underfoot, she was not worthy of leaving.

When Limestone suddenly opened her eyes again, she found herself lying in a hospital bed, the sunlight from the window gazing upon her. She surveyed her inner self and felt that a part of her was missing, replaced by something else familiar. She believed that her final weakness had been forever left in that infusion chamber, and it was hatred that allowed her to survive and lead all ponies forward.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_73_o0]
Now, Limestone Pie had become the embodiment of fire and fury.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_74]
ghost in the battlefield

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_74_desc]
In the beginning, there were sporadic reports from soldiers on the battlefield with the rock farm, claiming to have seen a swift-moving shadow destroying our tanks and camps during the night. However, these reports increased over the course of nearly a month and were no longer confined to the night or the battlefield. Soldiers described it in various ways, and it severely impacted our morale. After systematic analysis by the intelligence department, we can generally conclude that the rock farm has developed a high-performance combat weapon, possessing the size of an ordinary pony and extremely high firepower.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_74_o0]
What the hell is this

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_75]
The Empire’s Visit

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_75_desc]
The two sides took their seats in the conference hall. After adjusting her attire, Dawn Crown spoke:

"This impromptu visit is somewhat sudden. Her Majesty the Empress has sent us to inspect the construction of the Rock Farm. She is deeply concerned about whether the ponies here are leading stable and happy lives. After your preliminary reception, I am pleased to see that this is indeed the case."

Upon hearing this, Maud Pie nodded gracefully. Limestone Pie snorted and turned her face away. Marble Pie fidgeted uneasily, as she had already guessed what the two envoys were about to say:

"However, on the other hand, we have heard that your parents are unwell, and we have been sent to offer all the assistance we can."

Before she could finish, Limestone Pie turned pale, spun around, and glared at Dawn Crown and Double Delight.

"What? How did you know about this?"

Maud Pie’s expression darkened. Seeing Marble Pie with her head lowered in silence, she sighed. She had already guessed what had happened, but she didn’t want to reprimand her.

"No need to wonder, Sister Limestone," Marble Pie suddenly raised her head and said. Limestone Pie looked at her in surprise. She had thought the one to speak up would be Maud Pie.

"You..."

Limestone Pie was about to say something when she noticed the two foreign ponies beside them. She realized this was not the time for an argument. Moreover, the Empire knowing about their parents had already become a fait accompli. She gritted her teeth and fell silent.

Dawn Crown raised a hoof and continued:

"We have the best medical equipment and the most outstanding doctors in all of Equestria. Her Majesty the Empress is deeply moved by your sisters’ filial piety and wishes to provide free medical services. She believes all ponies in Equestria should learn from your example. What a great harmony this is."

"These are medical supplies prepared for Fire Rock Pie and Mica, to demonstrate Her Majesty’s sincerity. As I mentioned, these are gifts."

She clapped her hooves, and a team of Imperial ponies appeared before the Pie sisters, carrying several small medical devices and first aid kits marked with the Red Cross.

"However, to cure your parents, they will still require further treatment. Some medical equipment is too large, and the number of doctors involved is too many, so..."

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_75_o0]
"You will need to agree to have your parents taken to the Empire."

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_76]
A sudden illness

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_77]
three Pie sisters

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_77_desc]
The three Pie sisters found a secluded room and sat on one side of a table, silent and still. The air was thick with tension.


Two officials from the Empire, accompanied by other officers from the quarry farm, began their further inspection. Of course, these two officials weren’t genuinely interested in inspecting the “backward” farm; they were merely using this opportunity to wait for their response.Marble Pie began to miss the little things of the Pie family, unable to hold back her sobs.Limestone Pie rolled her eyes. Marble Pie’s crying only made her more agitated. She was about to tell her to stop, but the words wouldn’t come out.

“No matter what identities we’ve been given, we’ll always be family,” Maud Pie broke the silence first. Marble Pie and Limestone Pie looked at her in surprise. However, Maud Pie didn’t elaborate further; she just left it at that.Limestone Pie was stunned, but she quickly snapped out of it. Understanding, she stood up. “Then I’ll go tell those two damn bastards that we agree,” she said.

Maud Pie gave a slight nod. It was an excruciating decision for the Pie family.Just as Limestone Pie braced herself to open the door and find the two officials, she collided with the attending doctor.“Your parents have regained some consciousness,” he said, breathing heavily.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_77_o0]
The three sisters exchanged glances and swiftly rushed toward the hospital rooms of Igneous Rock and Cloudy Quartz.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_78]
A sudden illness

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_78_desc]
Igneous Rock Pie lay in his hospital bed, awakened by the irregular beeping of nearby machines. He breathed heavily, each inhale filling his lungs with scalding steam, causing him to groan in discomfort. Summoning all his strength, he coughed twice, which provided a slight relief. However, when he struggled to open his eyes, he saw the Empire’s insignia. Attempting to sit up, a nurse quickly stopped him, warning that it was too dangerous. He looked to the other side; his wife, who had shared his life, remained unconscious.
"Call the children," he rasped.

Soon, the Pie sisters gathered at his bedside. Marble Pie, overjoyed, exclaimed, "Father!" She leaped to his side, crying uncontrollably. Limestone Pie and Maud Pie watched the scene with pained expressions.

"How did I end up with such unfilial fillies?" Igneous Rock Pie suddenly shouted at them.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_78_o0]
The three sisters were instantly stunned.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_79]
Igneous Rock and sisters

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_79_desc]
Limestone Pie and Maud Pie exchanged glances, both stunned by their father’s unexpected words. Marble Pie lifted her tear-filled eyes, gazing at her father in shock, forgetting to wipe the snot and tears from her face.

"You... shouldn’t have handed the farm’s future to the Empire for my sake," Igneous Rock Pie said slowly, his earlier realization dawning on him.

"Limestone ... Maud... Marble... and my little Pinkamina..." he continued, "Having you as my daughters in this life... is my fortune. But..." He shook his head with effort. "You shouldn’t have given up your lives for me, and you certainly shouldn’t have colluded with those murderers who harmed Pinkamina..." His voice was weak but filled with conviction. "Look ahead, my children."

"Father!" Marble Pie cried out again, her sobs intensifying. Maud Pie lowered her head in silence, and Limestone Pie’s face turned crimson. She hated herself, hated her current helplessness.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_79_o0]
Soon, Igneous Rock Pie fell unconscious once more.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_80]
Disagreements Among the Sisters

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_80_desc]
Leaving the hospital room, the Pie sisters found themselves in an unusual argument. The unanimous decision they had just made evaporated the moment Igneous Rock Pie spoke.
Lumen LearningLimestone Pie remained adamant about sending their parents to Canterlot. Although the earlier scene had deeply pained her, it at least proved that the Empire might have the capability to heal them.However, Maud Pie chose to honor their parents’ wishes. At this moment, the greater good should prevail. If the quarry farm truly became an annex of the Empire, it would only make the farm and the remaining resistance fighters feel more despondent and helpless.
In reality, both sisters understood each other’s perspectives. They just couldn’t abandon their own stances.Marble Pie had remained silent. This was an issue for her two older sisters to consider. As the youngest, she didn’t know what decision to make. She looked at both sides until Limestone Pie suddenly spoke.

"Marble Pie, what do you think?" Limestone Pie, who had been arguing with Maud Pie just a moment ago, now turned to her.

"I... I..." Marble Pie panicked instantly.

"It’s okay, Marble Pie, we'll listen to you," Maud Pie said with a forced smile, her tone calm, as she placed a hoof around Marble Pie’s waist to encourage her to speak.Marble Pie glanced at her two sisters and then at their parents, who were once again on the brink of death. She steeled herself, closed her eyes, and softly said, "I want... I want... you said, we will always be Pie family ponies."Maud Pie was stunned. She felt a pang of disappointment but quickly nodded at Limestone Pie.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_80_o0]
The Pie sisters decided to tentatively agree to the Empire’s request.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_81]
High Above the Clouds

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_81_desc]
When Igneous Rock Pie awoke once more, he guessed it was another loud noise that had disturbed him. However, this time, the noise wasn’t the strange beeping of medical equipment but the deafening roar of steam engines. His body felt the same as before; the air in his lungs burned like fire, scorching his entire being. He slowly opened his eyes and looked around. A window above his head reflected the drifting clouds outside onto his wife, Cloudy Quartz, who lay quietly beside him with a gentle smile. Some tubes extended from her body under the blanket into equipment similar to his own.

"Cloudy Quartz?" he called weakly, but his faint voice was drowned out by the sound of the steam engines. He opened his eyes wider and tried to look around. When he saw the red insignia, a chill ran down his spine, confirming his earlier suspicion: his daughters hadn’t followed his instructions. Instead, they had agreed to the Empire’s plan to put him on the plane. He didn’t want to know what kind of agreement his daughters had made with the Empire, but he knew that if even Limestone Pie, who despised the Empire, had agreed, it must have something to do with him and Cloudy Quartz. At this moment, they were both in a small cabin, with no other medical ponies in sight.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_81_o0]
He struggled to sit up. As soon as he did, a sharp pain shot through his lungs.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_82]
Floating Among the Clouds

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_82_desc]
However, when Igneous Rock Pie gazed out at the beautiful scenery beyond the window, all his pain seemed to dissipate, as if carried away by the drifting wind. The airship he was aboard floated amidst the clouds, and the sun’s gentle rays bathed his face from such a close distance. This was his first time—and likely his last—being so high up. In his youth, he had briefly envied the idea of becoming a pegasus, imagining the city in the clouds as described by other ponies. Yet, decades of farm life had softened his edges, and he had come to accept that. He chuckled softly, shaking his head, thinking, "If only Cloudy Quartz could see this."

Soon, as if making a firm decision, he struggled to roll off the bed. The tubes inserted into his body were forcefully ripped out, sending a sharp pain through him. Blood began to flow from his wounds, and he nearly lost consciousness again. He coughed violently while crawling toward Cloudy Quartz’s bed, leaving a trail of blood on the wooden carpet beneath him.

"Cloudy Quartz?"

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_82_o0]
He reached her wife’s bedside, calling her name over and over.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_83]
Igneous Rock and Cloudy Quartz

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_83_desc]
Although his wife remained asleep and unresponsive, Igneous Rock Pie couldn’t help but smile as he gazed at her serene face. "You really should see this with your own eyes," he murmured. "Our daughters have brought us up to the clouds. You can’t even see our farm from here." He chuckled softly, a rare moment of levity.As he spoke, he gently removed the IV tube from Cloudy Quartz, tears finally escaping from the corners of his eyes. His voice grew faint and slurred from weakness."Do you remember the Pairing Stone? The moment I first saw you, I knew—I just knew I was meant to be with you. When I heard you liked rock candy made from sedimentary rocks, I offered you my most treasured collection..." Igneous Rock Pie reminisced, holding Cloudy Quartz’s hoof.

"Such wonderful memories," he said, glancing out the window once more as the deafening roar gradually faded.

"Igneous Rock..."

Turning his head, he saw that Cloudy Quartz had suddenly awakened, her eyes open and still wearing a gentle smile.

"Little Pinkamena is here too. How lovely..." Cloudy Quartz looked past Igneous Rock Pie, smiling.

He didn’t turn around; instead, he softly kissed her hoof.

"I love you."

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_83_o0]
"I love you too."

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_84]
Sudden Turn of Events

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_84_desc]
In the early morning,Dawn Crown was lying down enjoying a beauty spa treatment, contemplating how to report back to the young alicorn. Her moment of leisure was abruptly interrupted when the cucumber slices on her eyelids were suddenly lifted, and Double Delight’s anxious voice shattered the last bit of tranquility.

"Something’s wrong! Something’s wrong! Igneous Rock Pie and Cloudy Quartz!" Double Delight paced nervously in front of her, struggling to find the right words.

"Can’t this wait until we reach Canterlot to discuss how to handle those two?"Dawn Crown replied, somewhat annoyed. "If you're asking about what to do with those old ponies, honestly, we've deceived the Pie sisters. The medical experts told me they couldn’t guarantee a full recovery anyway. But this aligns with Her Majesty’s intentions."

At that moment,Dawn Crown and Double Delight were still aboard the royal airship, just about ten minutes away from Canterlot. Standing at the front of the airship, they could already see the city nestled on the mountainside in the distance.

"That’s exactly what I wanted to talk about!" Double Delight exclaimed.

 Dawn Crown’s heart skipped a beat. "What... what happened? Don’t tell me..."

Double Delight quickly nodded.

"Why didn’t anypony inform me earlier? Where are the nurses responsible for their care?"Dawn Crown’s anger flared.

"The nurses said they saw both of them unconscious and decided to take a short break. But just ten minutes later, when they returned to the ward, they found Igneous Rock Pie had torn off his equipment and was kneeling, covered in blood, beside Cloudy Quartz’s bed. And... he had even turned off her medical equipment..."

"The nurses tried to resuscitate them immediately, but it was already too late."

Upon hearing this,Dawn Crown broke into a cold sweat, experiencing a mix of shock and dread. The entire imperial plan was now in disarray. If the young alicorn found out, she might reduce her to ashes in a fit of rage or, at the very least, send her back to the quarry farm as a scapegoat. She glanced at the clock in the room—the airship was about to land, and she had little time left to think.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_84_o0]
"Those two damned old ponies!"

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_85]
Limestone Pie Takes the Stage

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_85_desc]
The power struggle at the rock farm had come to an end. The eldest of the Pie sisters, Limestone Pie, replaced her sister Maud Pie, declaring herself the new leader who would guide not only the Pie family but also the Apple family forward. However, due to her extremely volatile and unstable personality, as well as her less-than-stellar track record, outsiders remained concerned about her capabilities and foreign policies, speculating that she might initiate a new round of conflict between the rock farm and the Empire at any moment.

Recently, Limestone Pie issued a public statement, openly declaring that the previous rumors about her parents’ deaths and Maud Pie’s disappearance had no connection with the Empire. This move aimed to demonstrate her loyalty and willingness to cooperate with the Empire, breaking the external stereotype of her.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_85_o0]
Hopefully, the Empire will take the bait.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_86]
Limestone Pie Takes the Stage

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_86_desc]
The power struggle at the rock farm had come to an end. The eldest of the Pie sisters, Limestone Pie, replaced her sister Maud Pie, declaring herself the new leader who would guide not only the Pie family but also the Apple family forward. However, due to her extremely volatile and unstable personality, as well as her less-than-stellar track record, outsiders remained concerned about her capabilities and foreign policies, speculating that she might initiate a new round of conflict between the rock farm and the Empire at any moment.

Recently, Limestone Pie issued a public statement, openly declaring that the previous rumors about her parents’ deaths and Maud Pie’s disappearance had no connection with the Empire. This move aimed to demonstrate her loyalty and willingness to cooperate with the Empire, breaking the external stereotype of her.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_86_o0]
Hopefully, the Empire will take the bait.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_87]
Airship Catastrophe

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_87_desc]
"Your Majesty, the airship is on fire!" Upon hearing this alarming news, Cozy Glow was startled and quickly flew down from her seat. "Which airship?" she asked anxiously in her youthful voice, though she already knew the answer all too well, clinging to a sliver of hope.

"The one you dispatched to the rock farm," replied the soot-covered unicorn.

Without hesitation, Cozy Glow cast a teleportation spell. A burst of intense magical light enveloped her, and in an instant, she arrived at the scene of the accident.The area was desolate. The airship had crashed minutes earlier, debris scattered everywhere. Occasional explosions erupted from within the wreckage. Some ponies, supporting each other, screamed as they crawled out from the wreckage.

"Where are Dawn Crown and the others?" Cozy Glow urgently inquired of the escaping ponies. They shook their heads in terror, indicating they hadn’t seen them escape.

Without delay, Cozy Glow closed her eyes. A dazzling light burst from her horn, causing her mane to float as if defying gravity. A magical aura rapidly enveloped the entire, nearly hundred-meter-long airship. Everypony present was awestruck; many immediately knelt, barely daring to breathe.Within the aura, the flames visibly diminished, and the relentless explosions ceased. Soon, Cozy Glow slowly opened her eyes and, alongside the arriving Canterlot fire brigade, rushed into the wreckage to search for survivors.She found Dawn Crown lying in a room, covered in soot. Cozy Glow rescued her.The subsequent investigation could only speculate that the crash resulted from a malfunction in the landing system or the newly installed engine, as everything happened too quickly. Similar malfunctions weren’t uncommon in this new airship model, but such a severe accident had never occurred before.

What unsettled Cozy Glow the most was the confirmation that Igneous Rock Pie and Cloudy Quartz had perished in the accident—an outcome far beyond her expectations.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_87_o0]
This incident reignited internal concerns within the Empire regarding the safety of the new airship models.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_88]
Catastrophe of the Golden Stable Airship

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_88_desc]
The Empire’s pride, the newly commissioned Golden Stable airship, met an unexpected and tragic end today when it exploded while attempting to land in Canterlot.

This airship boasted luxurious interiors and exteriors, equipped with steam engines and various modern modifications developed by the Empire to enhance its speed. Previously, it had been used by imperial officials for visits across the Empire.

The accident resulted in dozens of pony casualties. The Empire is currently attempting to suppress any information related to the incident. Reports suggest that the airship was carrying some mysterious cargo, but all of it has now been completely incinerated.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_88_o0]
Deepest sympathies? Not really!

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_88_o1]
What a disaster.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_88_o2]
Oh my, is it the airship I was thinking of?

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_89]
The Siege of Canterlot

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_89_desc]
Limestone Pie led the charge against Canterlot, commanding her troops in a renewed assault. The remaining Imperial soldiers fought desperately, but Limestone couldn’t afford to wait for the heavy artillery to arrive. She led a contingent of soldiers, charging at the forefront.

As one of her squads reached the next intersection ahead of her, a sudden burst of blood erupted from a hidden sniper’s shot, and the soldier collapsed, convulsing on the ground. The concealed firing point had been well-placed. The wounded soldier’s anguished cries filled the air as he looked at Limestone with terror. Unfazed, Limestone signaled to a nearby unit with a hoof gesture, ordering them to fill the gap left on the battlefield. She cared little for her own life or that of her soldiers.

By nightfall, only the royal palace in Canterlot remained unconquered. Various units surrounded it completely. The anti-magic barrier was activated; while it had little effect on alicorns, it provided some psychological comfort to the troops. Maud Pie struggled to suppress her impulsive and urgent emotions. She wanted nothing more than to personally reduce that cursed alicorn to a pulp, but she knew she was no match for her.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_89_o0]
Limestone Pie issued the final order to attack.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_90]
Victory in War?

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_90_desc]
Once the heavy artillery was in position, Limestone Pie gave the command. The soldiers and tanks around her shouted her name and that of the Pie family as they charged into the palace. The roar of cannons echoed as Canterlot’s spires crumbled, each thunderous crash signaling the Empire’s downfall.

To her dismay, an hour later, the soldiers effortlessly raised the farm’s flag atop the last remaining half-ruined tower of the palace. However, the Emperor had long since vanished without a trace, and the remaining guards surrendered entirely. The war was over.

Limestone Pie forced the unarmed surrendered soldiers to stand together and then executed them one by one in a brutal manner to vent her inner resentment.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_90_o0]
The onlookers were all terrified.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_91]
Siege of Canterlot

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_91_desc]
The quarry farm’s army launched a new assault on Canterlot. Most of the soldiers had already surrendered, but the remaining Imperial troops were fiercely resisting. Heavy weaponry had yet to fully enter the battlefield. Limestone Pie, clad in Rockbreaker heavy armor, led a squad of soldiers at the forefront.

As one of her vanguard units reached the next intersection ahead of her, a sudden burst of blood erupted from the soldier’s body, causing them to collapse and convulse on the ground. A concealed firing point had been lying in wait. The wounded soldier emitted agonized wails, eyes filled with terror as they looked toward Limestone Pie. She remained expressionless, signaling to another platoon nearby to immediately fill the gap on the battlefield.

It was evident that the siege would persist for some time. Limestone Pie couldn’t tolerate the sluggish pace of the regular troops; every wasted minute increased the likelihood of Cozy Glow’s escape.

Unable to suppress her impulsive and urgent emotions any longer, she yearned to personally reduce that accursed alicorn to minced meat. There was no time to wait for the main force. She promptly assembled a team of elite Rockbreakers to follow her lead. Braving a hail of bullets, they weaved through various battlefields, heading straight for the royal palace without hesitation.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_91_o0]
She had only one thought in mind: Cozy Glow must not be allowed to escape.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_92]
Fated Confrontation

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_92_desc]
Limestone Pie and her team of Rockbreakers arrived at the palace shortly after, charging toward Cozy Glow’s stronghold. Limestone couldn’t recall the last time she'd been here; back then, the alicorn sisters still reigned, the sky was clear, and the palace’s grand stained-glass windows depicted her sister Pinkie Pie with pride. She pulled herself from the memories—Cozy’s palace doors were sealed shut.With a tactical hoof signal, the Rockbreakers executed their plan, swiftly breaching the entrance. Inside, Cozy Glow was preparing a teleportation spell to escape.

The Rockbreakers stormed in, spreading out to form a semi-circle. Limestone Pie entered slowly; this was the moment she'd longed for—her most despised enemy stood before her.

"Limestone Pie? Ha! I didn’t expect you to be so foolish," Cozy sneered upon recognizing the armored mare, clearly underestimating her. Though today might mark her downfall, she hadn’t anticipated dragging someone else down with her.

"Just you and your little toys? I don’t have time for games. But I admit, you've won this war. Let your death be my final gift to your army." She laughed maniacally. Limestone Pie watched silently, unmoved.

Suddenly, Cozy Glow unleashed a powerful blast of magic toward Limestone Pie. The shockwave filled the hall with dust, and a fierce beam of energy pierced the castle, reaching the sky, followed by the rumble of collapsing structures.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_92_o0]
As the dust settled...

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_93]
The Empress’s End

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_93_desc]
Cozy Glow stared in shock at Limestone Pie. Blood streamed down Limestone’s cheeks and features, her armor battered beyond recognition, with shards embedded in her body. Yet, she remained standing, catching her breath and regaining composure.Limestone raised her head, refusing to give Cozy a second chance. She lunged forward, delivering a decisive blow. Cozy, caught off guard, felt an unprecedented dizziness as blood spurted from her mouth. Her body, shattered like stone, crashed heavily against a broken pillar.

Limestone approached step by step. Cozy scrambled backward, attempting to fly, but her wings collapsed limply against her back. She closed her eyes, muttering a teleportation spell, but a sudden surge of pain overwhelmed her, breaking her concentration. Limestone was methodically tearing off her wings.

"Please, don’t kill me," Cozy Glow sobbed. Gone was the lofty Empress of Equestria; she was now just a frightened filly. Limestone lifted her like a rabbit.

"What hell are you?" Cozy cried louder, "I was totally wrong! I'm sorry for all the harm I've caused your family. Let me face justice." Her pleas intensified as she saw a spring-loaded bayonet extend from Limestone’s hoof armor, aiming for her horn.

Cozy’s screams and the surge of magic echoed throughout Canterlot. On the battlefield, soldiers collectively lowered their weapons, stunned. Realizing what had transpired, imperial troops emerged from trenches, surrendering. When the main forces reached Cozy’s palace, they found only blood and remnants.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_93_o0]
Limestone Pie stood amidst the carnage, licking blood from her blade.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_94]
Post-War Summit

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_94_desc]
The starry night sky gently parted a corner of the curtain. Starlight Glimmer anxiously peered outside, her gaze fixed on the chaotic square below. Ponies shouted and waved banners, clashing with soldiers attempting to maintain order. Their anger wasn’t directed at her; all eyes were on the gray figure now entering the building.

"Has she arrived?" Starlight turned to glance at Sunset Shimmer, who nodded solemnly. Starlight sighed and pulled the curtain back into place.

The heavy doors to the hall creaked open, and Starlight held her breath. The doors slammed shut with a resounding thud, and the room fell into an eerie silence. Starlight could hear her own heartbeat.

Limestone Pie sat quietly beside her, observing the gathering with a cold, calculating gaze. Thankfully, Unordered hadn’t arrived yet. Starlight had deliberately sent him away earlier, giving him an excuse to "host his Imperial Destruction Heavy Metal Party" elsewhere. Dealing with Limestone was already enough of a headache.

"Congratulations," Starlight began, forcing a smile. "The remnants of the Empire are scattering. Now we can rebuild Equestria’s future together."

Limestone’s lips curled into a sneer. "But the mastermind is still at large," she retorted coldly, her voice laced with bitterness.

Starlight nodded, her expression weary. "The Resistance is conducting a thorough search of Canterlot and the surrounding areas. But with her magical prowess, she could be anywhere. If she’s chosen to disappear, it could take a long time to find her."

"We will ensure she can never rise again," Limestone declared, her tone unwavering. Starlight felt a brief sense of relief; perhaps Limestone still valued their shared cause. But her next words shattered that hope.

"We will obliterate the Empire, erase every trace of it. Anypony who collaborated with the Empire will face the harshest judgment. Those who served in the Empire’s military will be imprisoned and made to atone until death."

Before Starlight could respond, Fireflash interjected, his voice stern. "That’s extreme. The Pie and Apple families accepted the Empire’s rule and became autonomous regions. Does that make them 'collaborators’ in your eyes?"

Limestone glared at Fireflash, her piercing gaze intensified by the reflection in her sunglasses. The room erupted into heated arguments.

"Enough!" Starlight cast a silencing spell, the soft blue glow calming the room. She wished she hadn’t broken the anger containment jar she once used on Trixie.

As the spell lifted, Limestone opened her mouth to speak. But Sunset Shimmer subtly shook her head, silently urging restraint.

"Don’t use your magic on me, unicorn," Limestone sneered. "You may think you understand my sisters, but I assure you, I'm nothing like them."

"The war against the Empire is over," Limestone continued, her voice cold. "The Resistance Alliance is no longer necessary. I will erase every trace of the Empire and capture that vile queen. Whether you join me or not is irrelevant. But heed this warning: do not stand in my way."

With that, she stood and exited the hall, leaving a trail of tension in her wake.

Starlight sighed, her heart heavy. Limestone was but a reflection of the pain many ponies felt. Some might never recover from the war.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_94_o0]
Regardless of Limestone’s departure, the meeting continued...

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_95]
Post-War Summit

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_95_desc]
A sliver of starlight peeked through the curtains, casting a nervous glow as Starlight Glimmer cautiously observed the plaza outside. Ponies were shouting and waving banners, clashing with soldiers attempting to maintain order. They weren’t here for her; all their ire was directed at the gray figure now entering the building below.

"Has she arrived?" Starlight glanced at the seated Sun Glimmer, who nodded before sighing and drawing the curtains closed.

Moments later, the door to the conference room was forcefully pushed open. Starlight held her breath as the heavy door slammed against the walls before closing with a resounding thud. The room fell into an eerie silence, the sound of her own heartbeat filling the air.

Limestone Pie sat quietly beside her, observing Starlight, Sun Glimmer, and the members of the resistance. At least Unordered wasn’t here today. Starlight had deliberately sent him away to "host his Empire-Destroying Heavy Metal Party," knowing his presence would only add to the tension.

"Congratulations, the Empress and her supporters have been defeated, and the remnants of the Empire are scattering." Starlight forced a smile. Indeed, this was a victory worth celebrating, but the celebrations had already occurred weeks ago. Today’s gathering was for a different purpose.

The room remained oddly quiet. Starlight noticed no pony was looking at her; all eyes were on Limestone Pie, some even with a hint of fear.

"Yes, the rumors are true." Limestone’s voice was cold and filled with dark satisfaction. "I personally tore that Empress apart like paper." She chuckled menacingly.

A chill ran down Starlight’s spine. Had this mare fallen as far as Queen Chrysalis?

"We thank Limestone Pie for... for bringing Cozy Glow to justice." Starlight’s voice trembled slightly. "She... ensured Cozy Glow met her deserved end." She paused, searching the room for support. None came.

Perhaps sensing the unease, Limestone spoke again. "But this is just the beginning." She leaned forward, her tone dark. "We will crush the Empire and any who defy harmony." She listed enemies, her voice growing colder with each name.

Before she could continue, a timid yet firm voice interrupted.

"We are not your 'disgusting bugs’!" Ocellus stood, her wings slightly spread in defiance.

"Respectfully, Miss Pie," Firefly adjusted her sunglasses and added, "based on your actions and those of your subordinates, I believe you have as much claim to speak of harmony as the Empress did."

The room erupted into chaos.

"Enough!" Starlight cast a silencing spell, the soft blue glow calming the room. She wished she hadn’t broken the anger containment jar she once used on Trixie.

However, the spell seemed to bounce off Limestone Pie, who sneered.

"Don’t use your magic on me, unicorn." Limestone’s voice dripped with disdain. "You may think you understand my sisters, but you're wrong." She stood, her presence imposing.
fanfiction.ws

"The war is over." She paced, her words sharp. "The resistance is obsolete." She glared at each pony in the room. "I will show you that only I can bring a new dawn to Equestria." With that, she stormed out, leaving a trail of tension in her wake.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_95_o0]
Regardless of Limestone’s departure, the meeting continued...

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_96]
A sudden illness

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_97]
A sudden illness

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_98]
The Invitation and the Medical Report

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_98_desc]
It had been quite some time since the airship’s visit, and no matter how hard the Pie sisters pressed for news of their parents, the Empire remained silent—no word was ever passed along. Their worries deepened like perlite sinking into still water. At dawn one morning, an imperial special train glided quietly into the quarry station. A squad of imperial envoys, cloaked in black, leapt down and hurried toward City Hall.

An hour later, a slim, rectangular package lay on the round table. Maud Pie and Limestone Pie exchanged glances, but neither made to open it.
“What do you suppose is inside?” Maud asked.
“This isn’t the Empress’s usual style,” Limestone replied. “If the Empire truly returned, they wouldn’t want outsiders to know.” She watched Maud unfurl the package as if inspecting a curious stone. “It can’t be anything good.”

Limestone’s voice dropped low, laced with a simmering anger—both sisters understood what lay behind their dread: the fate of their parents. Steeling herself, Limestone carefully cut open the package and read aloud:

    To Limestone Pie and the loyal members of the Pie family:
    Since the dawn of the New Era, our quarry farms have stood as paragons of imperial autonomy—nurturing the prosperity of all ponies and laying the groundwork for greatness. Your family’s renowned filial piety moves me deeply. Though I reign from the highest throne, there is much to admire in your example. Hence, with genuine goodwill, I have arranged care to relieve your parents’ suffering.

    Good news: Your parents have turned from the brink of death and are now under the diligent watch of professional healers. They eagerly await reunion with you.

    By imperial decree,
    Empress Cozy Glow

Maud folded the slender invitation shut. The other documents—medical reports for Igneous Rock Pie and Cloudy Quartz—were strewn on the table. Limestone flipped through them, brow furrowed. Unfamiliar medical jargon and cryptic data leapt from the pages, mingled with odd wafts of lavender and charred sage. A bright-red imperial seal stamped each report, as if to guarantee its authenticity.

Once Maud finished reading, she gathered the papers with care and placed them back on the table. Seeing Maud remain calm, Limestone’s nerves snapped—she swept the envelopes and reports into the air, letting them flutter wildly around the room.

“Have you seen the news, Maud? Listen: I don’t know what the Empress is plotting. That blasted airship… Father, Mother—they might already be… and now she’s dangling this as a trap!”

Her voice cracked, raw with emotion. At the mention of their parents, Limestone’s anger gave way to tears and trembling words. “But… what if this is true? We need certainty before our next step. We can’t cling to false hope and lose our chance at the right decision.”

Taking a steadying breath, Maud bent to pick up the scattered papers. “Are you mad? It’s obviously a scheme by those tyrants. I’m leaving for Appleloosa to warn Braeburn—we’ll ready ourselves for war against the Empire.”

Limestone couldn’t hold back any longer. With a crash, she shoved open the door and turned to go, tears streaming down her cheeks. She covered her face with her mane and sank to the floor, chastened by her own harshness.

Slowly, Maud knelt and drew Limestone into a tight embrace—perhaps the last one they’d share. After a moment, Limestone whispered through her sobs, “I’m sorry… I can’t lose you too.”

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_98_o0]
“I promise I’ll come back.”

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_98_o1]
“Take care, Maud… this time, I’m going.”

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_99]
Journey to Canterlot

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_99_desc]
Maud Pie and Mudbriar rode back to Canterlot on the special commissioner’s train alongside the visiting Imperial officials. From the moment they boarded, several Imperial agents in black uniforms stared unblinkingly at their every move. Maud Pie, however, paid them no mind and simply gazed out at the swirling snow. Her breath fogged the glass, tracing a thin veil over the grand buildings becoming clearer on the mountainside below.

Leaning her head on Mudbriar’s shoulder, she asked softly, “Once Father and Mother recover, will you marry me?”
Mudbriar cleared his throat and, with solemn deliberation, replied, “After rigorous analysis from geopolitical dynamics to neurocircuit psychology, although proposing to you now would impose substantial short‑term costs on the quarry farm, this action is not only macroscopically feasible but also promises positive shifts in irrational emotions and biological well‑being. …”

Maud Pie closed her eyes, smiling as she listened to Mudbriar’s earnest, cascading arguments. Outside, the wind’s howl faded to a gentle whisper.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_99_o0]
Before long, the train rolled into its final station.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_100]
Audience with the Empress

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_100_desc]
Maud Pie and Mudbriar made their way down the dark, seemingly endless corridor, trailed like shadows by the Empire’s operatives. They’d barely stepped off the train when they were informed this was a secret mission. Igneous Rock Pie and Cloudy Quartz had already been whisked away to a secluded treatment facility, and Cozy Glow herself was supposedly waiting to receive them. But Maud Pie knew from the moment her carriage left the quarry farm that she was no longer in control of her own fate.

Two guards slid open a heavy door. Inside, there was no sign of Rock Pie or Cloudy Quartz—only rows of fully armed soldiers flanking either side, standing at rigid attention. On the throne before them sat a small figure, whose youthful voice rang out:
“Welcome to Canterlot!”

Cozy Glow’s tone dripped with self-satisfaction as she addressed Maud Pie and Mudbriar. In the dim light, her golden crown flickered atop her head, barely sustaining the crumbling façade of her authority. Empress of all Equestria, victor of the Final Battle, usherer in the New Era—she sat high above them, smug and unchallenged.

“Your Majesty,” Maud Pie replied coolly, “I don’t much like you, and I certainly don’t wish you well.”
A ripple of tension ran through the black-clad operatives behind her. Their shifting feet and clenched lips were an unspoken warning—but Maud Pie didn’t flinch.

Cozy Glow’s grin froze for a moment before she forced out a laugh.
“Oh, how charming. You’ve come from your shabby farm to witness my greatness in person. Canterlot has been reborn under my rule.”

“Forgive my bluntness, Your Highness,” Maud Pie said, “but your taste is as muddled as a summer sugarcane field. You try to scare us, thinking you hold some grand advantage—bigger than the gap between your feigned maturity and your true age. Honestly, it’s… delusional.”

“Enough! Who dares mock me?” Cozy Glow’s face flushed red as she barked at Maud Pie and Mudbriar. Although Mudbriar stayed silent, he exchanged a knowing smirk with Maud Pie—they clearly weren’t intimidated.

“And what about Rock Pie and Cloudy Quartz?” Cozy Glow pressed, her tone turning ominous. “Don’t you want them to live?”

“So, what’s your endgame?” Maud Pie asked.

Cozy swapped back to her sweetest smile.
“I’ve changed my mind. The Pie family won’t have to foot the bills for Rock Pie and Cloudy Quartz’s treatments. You no longer need to toil in that backwater farm. Today, I offer you the return of your quarry farm’s autonomy to the Empire—in exchange, I guarantee every Pie family member a life of luxury here in Canterlot. You’ll even be reunited with your parents to enjoy family bliss.”

The moment her words fell, Imperial soldiers closed in, guns trained on Maud Pie and Mudbriar.

“Your dreams—and your rule—are as fragile as your crown. I know they’ve passed on,” Maud Pie said, her heart breaking yet her voice steady. Cozy Glow was taken aback; she hadn’t expected Maud to come here knowing the truth.

“Alright, fine,” Cozy stammered, “I didn’t plan for things to go this far… but now—it’s too late. You’d like to see your other kin, wouldn’t you? Must they all mourn with you to satisfy your grief?”

Ignoring the Empress, Maud Pie turned to Mudbriar and smiled. “My love for you is as enduring as bedrock.”

Mudbriar chuckled, brushing Maud Pie’s cheek with a hoof. “Actually, Poplar’s durability doesn’t match my love for you.”

“Enough! If you love stones so much, go be living sculptures!” Cozy Glow screamed, her mane shaking and floating in the surge of her magic. Her horn glowed brilliantly, illuminating the entire hall.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_100_o0]
The light faded—two young lives were frozen forever in that final moment.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_101]
No news

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_101_desc]
Since Maud Pie and Mudbriar left the farm, there had been no word from them. According to their agreement before departure, Limestone Pie knew what this silence meant. The Empire had once again taken a close family member from her, and she was powerless to stop it.

When the Empire sent a telegram, not only did it confirm the news, but it also falsely accused Limestone Pie of being a spy and betraying the Empire. She didn’t rush into a war that would play into their hands, nor did she, like her sister Marble Pie, spend day after day caressing Limestone Pie’s photo frame. Upon learning what had happened, Marble Pie cried without eating or drinking for three whole days and was now lying in a hospital bed.

At this point, there was no room left for Limestone Pie to grieve or choose. The rock farm needed the Pie family, and to avenge her sisters, the Pie family now required a fully operational war machine. What she needed most at this moment was patience and to avoid giving the Empire any possible excuse.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_101_o0]
Would the rock farm embark on an irreversible path?

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_102]
ownership of the two sisters’ castle

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_102_desc]
We are steadily taking over imperial lands from the collapsing Imperial Guard. However, the ownership of the Two Sisters Castle has become a problem. After the meteorite incident a few years ago, Cozy Glow dispatched a unit to control the area, aiming to keep the Apple family in check. Through years of meticulous planning by the Empire, it has been transformed into a formidable fortress.
Although the Apple Pie family has not officially negotiated this matter with us, should we take the initiative to return the Two Sisters Castle to them as a gesture of gratitude for our joint resistance? Or should we retain control of it for potential future needs?

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_102_o0]
Return the castle to them. They deserve it.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_102_o1]
It’s not the time yet.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_103]
starlight returns the castle

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_103_desc]
After steadily reclaiming the lost lands of Equestria, today, Starlight Glimmer announced that the Castle of the Two Sisters, previously occupied by the Empire, would be returned to us. With that, the wedge that had long been driven between Appleloosa and the rock farm has finally been removed once and for all.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_104]
Abolish the unequal treaties of the empire

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_104_desc]
We have cut off all ties with the empire and are no longer bound by its treaties

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_104_o0]
The flag of the empire will never appear on the land of the farm again!

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_105]
ownership of the two sisters’ castle

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_105_desc]
We are steadily taking over imperial lands from the collapsing Imperial Guard. However, the ownership of the Two Sisters Castle has become a problem. After the meteorite incident a few years ago, Cozy Glow dispatched a unit to control the area, aiming to keep the Apple family in check. Through years of meticulous planning by the Empire, it has been transformed into a formidable fortress.
Although the Apple Pie family has not officially negotiated this matter with us, should we take the initiative to return the Two Sisters Castle to them as a gesture of gratitude for our joint resistance? Or should we retain control of it for potential future needs?

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_105_o0]
Return the castle to them. They deserve it.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_105_o1]
It’s not the time yet.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_106]
A private conversation

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_106_desc]
Apple Bloom held her head in pain. Outside the window, the flag of Greater Rockville fluttered silently in the wind.

Mossy Scent wiped away her unstoppable tears, her mouth slightly open, wanting to say something comforting — but no words would come. In truth, she was the one who needed comfort the most.

Moments earlier, she had confessed everything — how she met Limestone Pie, and how Limestone had asked her to assassinate Braeburn. She had thought she would keep that secret buried forever. Or perhaps that revealing it might make her feel lighter. But neither happened.

Now, everything had gone far beyond what she could have imagined. As the one who set all of this in motion, she knew she had to bear the responsibility.

Limestone Pie, in the name of both the Apple family and the Pie family, had turned her wrath toward one nation after another. Peace, like an apple hanging from a tree, was always just within reach — yet forever unreachable.

She had changed. And so had Appleloosa, and the ponies working the stony soil of the quarry farm.

At Braeburn’s public funeral not long ago, Limestone Pie had stood before the crowd, falsely recounting how her deep and unwavering bond with him was destroyed by the Empire. Below the stage, countless ponies shouted her name again and again. The scene made Mossy Scent sick to her stomach — and terrified.

She was grateful, at least, that she was still alive. That she hadn’t been thrown into some lightless cell by Rockville’s Bureau of Public Affairs under a fabricated charge. Perhaps it meant Limestone Pie still trusted her — that she believed Mossy Scent would never betray her. Or maybe… Limestone truly saw her as family.

“She betrayed two families,” Apple Bloom whispered hoarsely. “She doesn’t deserve to be my sister anymore.”

She looked at Mossy Scent with those sorrowful, wide eyes.
“This isn’t your fault. At least… not yours alone.”

“No,” Mossy Scent said, trembling all over. “I know what I did. And it was that one thought — that single choice — that brought all of this to life.”

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_106_o0]
We must rescue them, by any means.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_106_TOOLTIP]
Apple Bloom will plan an uprising

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_107]
Failed persuasion

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_107_desc]
Apple Bloom knocked on John Bull’s door. Earlier that day, after Mossy Scent had temporarily returned, she had compiled a list of members of the Apple Pie family. To ensure the success of any potential plan, the truth could only be revealed to a few trusted relatives at first — to win their understanding and support.

Everything had gone well so far. Her brothers and sisters were furious when they heard the truth. But when Apple Bloom told this particular relative, she didn’t hear the answer she wanted.

“Take a walk outside, sister,” John Bull said calmly. “Soon, Appleloosa will have just as many skyscrapers as Manehattan. In just a few years, we’ll be strolling through a great city rising from the apple fields.

Our family has taken root here — and it’s Limestone Pie who made it grow. Ponies respect us because we’re part of the Apple Pie lineage. Our lives are richer now than they were before the war...

And yes, perhaps it was her misstep that led to Braeburn’s death — but I truly believe Limestone acted for the good of our family.”

Apple Bloom’s voice trembled as she cut him off.

“You’re clinging to a false prosperity! All of this — everything — is built on conspiracy and blood!”

John Bull sighed and shook his head.

“No, Apple Bloom. You must look further ahead.

If we overthrow Limestone Pie, when the ponies realize they’ve been deceived by her all this time, they might turn against our entire family. We could lose everything — and worse, plunge this land back into chaos and division.

And if that happens, the spark of the next war would come not from strangers… but from our own bloodline tearing itself apart.

Is that truly the outcome you want?”

Apple Bloom fell silent.
She finally realized this wouldn’t go as she had imagined.

Whether Limestone Pie was only satisfying her own twisted desires or not, the fact remained — she had brought prosperity to both families and admiration from ordinary ponies. To topple her could easily destroy everything the two families had built.

Even with the truth now known, not every family member would be willing to accept it.

Apple Bloom opened the door again and stepped out. She sighed.
There were too many questions to consider — and perhaps, this simply wasn’t the right time.

Limestone Pie had already begun mustering troops along the border. Everypony knew what she was planning. And when her ambition finally became undeniable, no matter how loudly she claimed to fight for the glory of the Apple family, Apple Bloom believed both families would, at last, stand against her.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_107_o0]
Perhaps what Limestone Pie did next would prove that he was completely wrong

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_107_TOOLTIP]
No matter what Apple Bloom is planning, she needs more patience...

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_108]
The last funeral

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_108_desc]
The bone-chilling raindrops, mixed with snowflakes and shards of ice, struck relentlessly against Apple Bloom’s black umbrella. This was the third funeral she had attended this month for a member of the Apple family.

Apple Bloom remembered the remains lying inside the finely crafted applewood coffin. She recalled how, whenever her sister Applejack took her to visit Apple Russet, he would always bake endless apple pies for her. But so many funerals had already drained the family’s tears — even she could no longer muster a single genuine drop for this poor relative.

Many members of the Apple family were lucky enough to attend the ceremony, though countless others were still fighting on the battlefield or stationed at forward command posts, unable to return. Below the stage, dozens of soldiers fired their rifles in salute. On the platform, one pony after another wept as they spoke of the past, while bouquets of fresh flowers were placed atop the lowering coffin.

For a member of the Apple Pie branch, he was considered fortunate. His hidden command post had been struck by a misfired shell, yet thanks to his status, he received such a complete — even luxurious — funeral ceremony, enjoying the company of his family one last time. Most nameless ponies, however, were still charging forward under Limestone Pie’s orders, eventually falling silent on the battlefield, left to the mercy of the wind and rain.

Many in the family knew something was terribly wrong with the current situation, but there was no better choice. The Great Rockville’s territory expanded day by day, and the prestige of Limestone Pie’s faction grew ever more dazzling — yet none of it had anything to do with the ponies living on this land.

When the funeral finally ended and the family members began to disperse, Apple Bloom made up her mind. She exchanged a glance with Mossy Scent, then stepped forward to stop everypony in their tracks.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_108_o0]
"Wait！ I have the truth of something to tell everypony."

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_108_TOOLTIP]
chance is coming...

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_109]
Journey to the Banquet

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_109_desc]
When several officers showed up in Apple Bloom’s presence carrying an invitation, she was startled at first. But after learning what it was about, panic began to set in. Limestone Pie had invited her to represent the Apple family at a multi-species friendship banquet. Besides the Apple family, guests would include parrots, buffalo, and ponies from several allied nations.

In the invitation, Limestone Pie wrote that she deeply missed Apple Bloom — she missed the warmth and joy of spending Hearth’s Warming Eve together with her and Applejack in the little house on the rock farm. Ever since their victory over the Empire, she hadn’t had a proper talk with the sister she cared about most.

Apple Bloom wasn’t ready to see Limestone Pie again, but she went anyway — she didn’t want Limestone to suspect anything.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_109_o0]
Apple Bloom boarded the train to the castle of the two sisters

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_110]
ownership of the two sisters’ castle

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_110_desc]
The waiter led her through the grand hall to the banquet venue. The place was already filled with many creatures dressed in splendid attire, dancing gracefully to the cheerful tunes of saxophones and brass instruments — melodies written by Pinkie Pie herself.

As Apple Bloom watched in awe, a mare smiled and waved at her — it was Limestone Pie. Several officials and envoys surrounded her, but there was no trace of menace on her face, only a smile — a seemingly simple and harmless smile. Apple Bloom barely had time to think; she quickly waved back. Limestone walked over and ruffled her mane gently.

“Look at you, you’ve grown so much since I last saw you,” Limestone said.

Apple Bloom didn’t know what to say. She just smiled faintly and lowered her head.

Limestone sighed softly. “You must’ve gone through a lot these past years. How are your friends doing? About your sister and brother… I’m truly sorry. But I promise, I’ve already punished those responsible.”

Though her tone sounded casual, there was still that familiar hint of fierceness hidden in her voice.

Apple Bloom thought — if she hadn’t known the truth, if she hadn’t met Moss Fragrance by chance, if she hadn’t gone through everything she did… maybe at this very moment she would’ve thrown herself into Limestone’s embrace and burst into tears. But now, she was far more mature than Limestone believed.

“Thank you, Sister Limestone. I’m fine, and so are my friends. I didn’t expect you to care so much about me,” Apple Bloom replied calmly, then gently hugged Limestone.

Limestone smiled again, as if satisfied with the answer. “No matter what, the hardest days are behind us. I hope you’ll enjoy tonight’s banquet. I’m proud to see you standing on your own now. You’re the rising star of our family, and I want to introduce you to our foreign guests — after all, you might be the next leader of Greater Rockville someday. I’d like you to stay here with me and help handle state affairs. There are many tasks I could entrust to you, and I dare say one day you’ll be even more beloved by ponies than I am.”

Her words struck Apple Bloom like a bolt of lightning. Fear crept into her heart. Did Limestone already know about her secret plans, and now intended to keep her here under soft confinement? Or… was she truly sincere, hoping to nurture her as a successor? Or perhaps staying close to Limestone would be the best way to uncover her true intentions and find solid evidence?

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_110_o0]
“I… I’m sorry, Sister Limestone… this is such a huge decision… I need some time to think about it.”

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_110_o1]
“Really? Thank you, Sister Limestone, for giving me this opportunity.”

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_111]
Refusing Limestone Pie

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_111_desc]
“I… I’m sorry,Sister Limestone … this matter… it’s too serious… I need some time to think about it,” Apple Bloom panted as she spoke.

“It’s alright. You can take your time to think about your future,” Limestone Pie placed a hoof on her shoulder. “There’s no need to rush your answer. For today, just enjoy the banquet. You must know—I’ll always love you…”

Apple Bloom nodded lightly. Limestone Pie kept talking, but her words only drifted faintly past Apple Bloom’s ears.

Maybe… maybe Limestone Pie truly cared for the family?
Maybe Braeburn’s death wasn’t entirely her fault?

Apple Bloom quickly shook her head, forcing those thoughts away. No—those were just Limestone Pie’s smokescreens. Even if she did care deeply for the Apple family and her, and even if she was a good sister in some ways, that could never erase the sins she had committed—the atrocities she inflicted on so many, and the ruthless heart that would stop at nothing to reach her goals.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_111_o0]
The banquet went on, but for Apple Bloom, it was already over.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_112]
Agree to Limestone

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_112_desc]
“Really? Thank you,Sister Limestone, for giving me this chance,” Apple Bloom said. Though she still held deep doubts toward Limestone Pie, staying close to her—and waiting for the right moment—was clearly the wiser move.

Hearing this, Limestone Pie once again showed a rare smile—one that, at least this time, seemed truly heartfelt.

“I was worried you might refuse,” she said warmly. “I’m so glad. Now, let me introduce you to some of the guests visiting today. Many of them can’t wait to meet you.”

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_113]
ownership of the two sisters’ castle

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_114]
Taking back Appleloosa

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_114_desc]
Apple Bloom stormed into Appleloosa’s town hall with dozens of members of the Apple Family at her side. The guards on duty, seeing this sudden and forceful intrusion, didn’t dare to stop them or even ask questions. All they could do was step aside and make way.

Soon, before Apple Bloom used Appleloosa’s broadcast tower to announce this shocking news to all of Equestria, the Apple Family members still working inside the town hall had already learned the truth—that Braeburn’s death had not been the work of the Empire, but rather an accident secretly orchestrated by Periwinkle’s faction.

Although some members of the Apple Family still hesitated and feared the power of Limestone’s group, most of them quickly rose up. They seized control of the nearby Appleloosa garrisons and declared independence from Greater Rockville. The Apple Family commanders of these units had, even before today, already received secret warnings and signals from ponies such as Mossy Scent.

When the flag of Greater Rockville was lowered and the Apple Family’s green star-and-apple banner was raised again, everypony in Appleloosa knew exactly what that meant.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_114_o0]
The uprising began.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_115]
Search for Limestone

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_115_desc]
When Appaloosa declared its separation from Greater Rockville, it seemed that none of the soldiers across the country had received any orders from Limestone Pie. Perhaps no pony wished to witness a civil war between the two families. However, more and more members of the Apple family joined Apple Bloom’s march toward the Two Sisters’ Castle.

They only hoped that Limestone Pie could give them an explanation — a reasonable answer for all her past actions. But there was nothing. The castle of the two sisters was utterly silent.

Now, Apple Bloom once again walked through the halls of the Two Sisters’ Castle. She remembered the day she had once been invited here by Limestone Pie to attend a banquet. Only this time, her company was not elegantly dressed guests, but fully armed soldiers.

The takeover of the castle caused little bloodshed — partly because of its proximity to Appaloosa. Many soldiers had already scattered before the army arrived, and most of those who remained surrendered without resistance.

Apple Bloom nervously pushed open the door to Limestone Pie’s office, but inside she found only an empty, ransacked room.

Marble Pie was hiding fearfully in one corner of the castle. When the soldiers found her, nopony treated her harshly. Apple Bloom only hoped Yuki could tell her where Limestone Pie had gone, but Yuki just kept shaking her head. Did even she not know?

For now, the urgent matter was dealing with the chaos Limestone Pie had left behind. The family members held a brief council, where Apple Bloom was appointed as the temporary new leader and charged with managing the government affairs.

Most of the castle’s officials soon returned to their posts, but as for the generals, nopony quite knew what to do with them. Apple Bloom simply sent them home — if any of them wished to follow the vanished Limestone Pie, she would “let them be.”

Though she hadn’t learned much from Limestone Pie before, Apple Bloom still tried her best to handle the mountain of work that had piled up over the past few days.

Besides Limestone Pie’s whereabouts, what concerned her most was whether she could gain support from Equestria. Negotiations had begun over the return of the unlawfully occupied lands, and at long last, the soldiers on the front lines could finally lay down their weapons.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_115_o0]
Where is she?

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_116]
The uprising failed.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_116_desc]
Apple Bloom had anticipated that this day might come, yet she still could not accept such a cold, harsh truth. She had never imagined that Limestone Pie could be so ruthless and merciless. Perhaps Limestone had sensed her plan from the very beginning, or maybe some member of the Apple Pie family had inadvertently revealed the secret.

When Appleloosa declared its independence, the initial shock quickly turned into disaster. Limestone Pie’s army launched a well-organized, massive assault. The uprising forces alone were powerless to resist.

What chilled Apple Bloom even more was that Limestone Pie delivered a speech that very night — not only denying everything she had done, but even accusing Apple Bloom of being a traitor to the Apple Pie family.

Now, the entire Apple Pie family had been split in two, and with every passing second, ponies were dying because of her. Limestone Pie was using this opportunity to eliminate any dissenting voices within the family, while the remaining Apple Pie members escorted Apple Bloom safely across the border.

Apple Bloom sat on the train, gazing back at Appleloosa’s night sky. Cannons roared, and the hot, thick smoke dimmed even the starlight. The moonlight still spilled over every apple tree. Apple Bloom knew it might be the last time she would ever see them.

Family bonds were being buried along with the memories of Appleloosa’s former beauty. All the past had been a facade carefully maintained by Limestone Pie. The thought plunged Apple Bloom into endless sorrow once more.

She remembered, years ago, when Pinkie Pie had discovered some clues in a family record. The two families had shared their first hearth night together. That night had been beautiful — not just with her, but with Applejack, Limestone Pie, Maud Pie, Marble Pie, and Pinkie Pie herself. They sang together, exchanged gifts — everything was so perfect.

Although Limestone Pie rarely spent time alone with her, rarely smiled at her, and often wore a cold, distant expression, Apple Bloom knew clearly that Limestone Pie had loved her as she would her own younger sister.

Could all those experiences have been false?

The final war may have not only changed the lives of every pony but also fundamentally altered their very characters.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_116_o0]
Nothing can change...

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_117]
alone

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_117_desc]
Limestone Pie tore the documents in front of her to pieces. When she realized that, apart from Marble Pie, the only pony she had ever truly considered a little sister — along with many members of the Apple Pie family — had ignited a wave of rebellion against her in Appleloosa, she felt, for a moment, as if she were on the verge of tears.

But quickly, that sadness and loss transformed into anger and bewilderment. The remaining flicker of love for family slowly dissipated.

Since Maud Pie and Mudbriar had passed away, Marble Pie had remained timid and hesitant. The Apple family had grown anxious, trapped in endless doubt and internal strife. Limestone Pie had almost single-handedly kept the quarry farm running, all while thrusting herself into the whirlpool of political intrigue — all for the day she could bring justice to her little sister and both families.

Except for the night she conquered Canterlot, Limestone Pie could hardly remember ever sleeping peacefully. She had sacrificed everything that could be sacrificed to secure victory in war, opening a new future for the Apple Pie family. Yet now, the closest ponies to her left her with no choice — just as she had left Braeburn.

It had also been her intention to remove Braeburn from the leadership competition for the Apple Pie family once and for all. She could not bear his repeated hesitation in the face of the Empire. Though various unforeseen events had completely diverted her original plans, it was not her fault; everything she did had been necessary to defeat the Empire.

There could be no division in Appleloosa or the quarry farm — neither before nor now. She acted for the good of the entire family. Why could they not understand?

Limestone Pie took a few deep breaths and gradually let go. Even if they could not understand, it did not matter. Greater Rockville had already become the greatest region in Equestria — clear proof of one simple fact: they only needed to obey. Ordinary ponies should never doubt what she had done.

Her hatred for the Empire had brought her to this point, winning a bright future for the farm, Appleloosa, and tens of thousands of ponies. Perhaps that same hatred toward ungrateful family members could inspire her to prove she had always been right. One day, new members of the Apple Pie family would thank her under the sunlit lands.

With this thought, Limestone Pie’s heart sank. She picked up a barely intact sheet of paper from the floor and hastily scribbled a few words. Then, she called to the trembling guards at the office door, ordering them to notify the other departments of her next arrangements — political and military alike.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_117_o0]
Maybe Limestone becoming a better version of herself

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_118]
a symbol

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_118_desc]
The castle had been used as a military base by the Empire years ago and had been fully renovated. After the fall of the Empire, the Apple Pie family’s political center was relocated to the space between the two sisters’ castles, where it underwent even more modern and stylish upgrades.

However, to respond to recent unexpected incidents and to gain wider attention, Limestone Pie decided to hold the symbolic ceremony at the quarry farm.

Departing from Rockville Town, the streets along the way were completely renewed. On either side, cheering crowds of ponies lined the roads, while photographers trailed for coverage and soldiers patrolled diligently.

Limestone Pie stepped down from the carriage and walked ahead alone. Sunlight poured over her as the sky above had been scrubbed clear. She cast a quick glance around as she continued forward. The crowds on either side continued to shout her name, louder and louder, until she felt a certain numbness.

A small pink filly waved the flag of Greater Rockville excitedly. Through the gray wall formed by the soldiers, she appeared at the edge of Limestone Pie’s vision. Her mane and coat — so much like… — and Limestone Pie’s heart skipped a beat.

She hurried over to that side of the road. Her sudden movement startled the surrounding soldiers and ponies. The pink filly was about to turn away, but Limestone Pie called out:

“Hey, child… wait!”

Ponies nearby all turned their heads toward the filly, freezing her in place. Photographers quickly adjusted their cameras to capture the best angle. Soldiers made space, and Limestone Pie slowly approached, smiling as she gently patted the filly’s head.

“Tell me, child, are you alright?”

The filly’s smile vanished completely, replaced by sheer fear.

“You’re not real,” the filly whispered in a small, sharp voice.

Limestone Pie forced a gentle smile again.

“Silly child, of course I’m real… hmm, do you want to take a picture with me?”

The filly shook her head.

“Mom said the Emperor doesn’t talk to ordinary ponies.”

“No, I’m not an emperor. I am the Protec…” Limestone Pie began hurriedly, but stopped mid-sentence. The filly had been frightened by her earlier demeanor and now cowered, head down, too scared to meet her eyes. Limestone Pie sighed. This age is too young to understand the complexities of reality, she thought. She comforted herself.

Finally, she managed a faint smile:

“Child, you remind me so much of my sister. You know, I really miss her.”

The filly gave no reply.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_118_o0]
Then, Limestone turned back dejectedly and continued walking down the street

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_119]
ownership of the two sisters’ castle

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_119_desc]
Limestone Pie walked onto the stage. Behind her stood rows of disciplined officers, most of whom had been promoted by her own hoof on the battlefield and had remarkable battle achievements. There were also scientific officials like the recently recovered Platinum, who had made outstanding contributions to advancing research levels comparable to Lomaqi and other regions.

On one side of the stage, led by her younger sister Marble Pie, stood many members of the Apple Pie family. Many of them had previously participated in Appleloosa’s uprising against Limestone Pie. Now, they served as a symbol — a symbol that those past rebellions were merely internal conflicts within the family and had already been resolved. No pony knew how Limestone Pie had persuaded them, or what conditions she had agreed upon.

Of course, Apple Bloom was not present, nor were Cheese Sandwich and the others. Although Limestone Pie had extended an invitation, they refused for minor, inconsequential reasons — a slight resentment that added to Limestone Pie’s weight of grievances.

Taking a deep breath, Limestone Pie began to speak slowly:

“Fifteen years ago, I was just an ordinary filly from a landbound family on this land. I was happy — I had three lovely younger sisters, and together we formed this family. Especially my sister Pinkie Pie, who brought laughter to all of Equestria. I never considered myself even a tenth as remarkable as she was.

Until that day came, everything changed. Pinkie Pie disappeared and never returned. The Empire did not give her back or offer us one answer we could believe. Our hometown fell into chaos, countless ponies were displaced, and my parents became gravely ill. Everything left me bewildered until my sister Maud Pie stood up in that moment of hardship and transformed the quarry farm into a town. At first I opposed it, but then I thought of how nearly every family had lost loved ones in the war, or, like us, still waited for news that never came. I began to treat every victim on this land as my new kin. Only then could we stand like basalt against the winter wind. I am glad I did.”

“Of course, I am nowhere near as outstanding as Maud Pie. I chose to step back, entrusting the future of the quarry farm to her. And in the meantime, she earned the recognition of all ponies — in western Equestria, Rockville, Pondrosa… I am glad that you too chose her. Together, we built a new unity, the embryo of a great nation.

In those dark years, we withstood the storm together… until the Empire destroyed everything again. They envied Maud Pie’s honor and achievements. They envied the thriving life of ponies on this land. They wanted us to remain in poverty and pain, bowing to the Empress every single day.

I would not allow this to happen. I knew that only I could point the way for all ponies at this moment. Otherwise, everything Pinkie Pie, Maud Pie, and Braeburn had built — the future of all ponies on this land — would collapse.”

“I am glad I succeeded. With me, and with so many ponies behind me — especially the Apple Pie family, this most sincere, kind, and brave family — the Empire was defeated, and the Empress, along with her portrait, turned to ash.

Yet I know this is not the end. Peace and happiness did not arrive immediately. Chaos and war still rage around Greater Rockville, ever watchful. I understand I cannot relax. I must lead everyone forward, and only I can do it.

But the path is not smooth. Remaining imperial agents and powerful enemies spread rumors about me and the Apple Pie family, trying to unravel our united hearts. I cannot allow this. Only I can guide Greater Rockville onward; otherwise, everything Pinkie Pie, Maud Pie, and Braeburn built — the future of all ponies — would crumble.”

“I am glad I did it. Although some recent events have been grave, I assure everyone that they have been satisfactorily resolved. The rubble and vines around and within Greater Rockville and the Apple Pie family are being cleared. There is still a long road ahead, but under my protection, I believe we are safe for now.

Therefore, I need everyone to continue to recognize me, to trust me unconditionally, and to know what I fight for. At the same time, I must clearly define my power and responsibilities, to protect everyone from the distractions that wear down the spirit. I also know what this means. I am still an ordinary member of the Apple Pie family — an ordinary landbound filly on this land. But to draw a clear line against conspirators outside the map, and to symbolize a new era, I have decided to grant myself a new title: Protector of the Nation. My term is eternal, and this title and responsibility are henceforth solemnly recorded in the laws of Greater Rockville.”

The entire celebration venue erupted in the sound of hoofbeats that would echo for generations. Cannons roared with thunderous blasts, while confetti and tiny gemstone dust soared into the sky. Ponies below shouted in unison:

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_119_o0]
Long live for Limestone!

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_119_TOOLTIP]
This is the end of her story. The PIHC production team thanks you for playing!

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_120]
A Chance Encounter with Marble Pie

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_120_desc]
Life in the political center of Greater Rockville had been going on for some time now. Looking back on how she had so decisively agreed to Limestone Pie’s request not long ago, Apple Bloom still felt a bit puzzled. Perhaps she had been moved by Limestone’s sincerity, or perhaps Limestone Pie was simply one of the few relatives she could rely on.

Yet, Apple Bloom’s thoughts still lingered on Braeburn. She intended to piece together the clues herself.

Limestone Pie had assigned Apple Bloom a series of trivial and simple tasks — most of them only requiring signatures or stamps. No matter how Apple Bloom judged them, they wouldn’t have a major impact. For now, she had no complaints.

She stretched lazily and took a walk through the castle. Limestone Pie was nowhere to be seen — perhaps discussing matters with some officers. She rarely spent the entire day here, making it hard to see her. Various officials passed through, many with Apple family bloodlines, so some would greet her politely. But most of these ponies were loyal supporters of Limestone Pie — not the ones Apple Bloom was seeking.

Finally, in a quiet corner, Apple Bloom found her: Marble Pie, the youngest of the four Pie sisters, and the younger sister of Maud Pie and Limestone Pie. Could she know something?

With that thought in mind, Apple Bloom cleared her throat and asked,

“Marble Pie, are you alright?”

Marble Pie hadn’t expected to see Apple Bloom here. She studied her with curiosity and softly replied,

“Hi?”

Apple Bloom nodded happily and then gave her youngest sister a gentle hug.

The two of them began chatting, sometimes hesitantly, sometimes in short bursts. Marble Pie gradually opened up. In such a tense environment, there were very few ponies willing to converse with her like this.

However, Apple Bloom did not ask about anything regarding Limestone Pie at that moment — it simply wasn’t the right time.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_120_o0]
This sister was even shyer than her younger sister.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_121]
A Midnight Fright

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_121_desc]
Apple Bloom was jolted awake by the clatter outside. A pair of armored steam-engine trucks rumbled past the castle; apart from not running on rails, they might as well have been trains. She yawned, rolled out from the soft bed, and glanced out the window. The moon still hung in the sky and for a moment it made her think of Princess Luna.

Apple Bloom pushed open the door. Ponies hurried to and fro in the corridors, and Limestone Pie was nowhere to be seen — but Apple Bloom already knew who she needed to find.

By the time Apple Bloom found Marble Pie, the sun had risen. Marble Pie told her that Limestone Pie had launched a military action against a neighboring nation during the night and had gone to the front herself. Everypony in the castle was busy dealing with the fallout.

“Aren’t you going? Why didn’t Sister Limestone bring you with her?” Apple Bloom asked, half-casually. Marble Pie was silent for a moment, then answered slowly, “I’m not a pony who’s good at giving orders.”

“But by rank, you’re still a general of the Great Rockville… of the Apple Pie family.”
“During the war I only handled logistics for the ponies, so after the Empire fell I gradually stepped away from the army…” Marble Pie trailed off. Apple Bloom didn’t press further; she just watched Marble Pie in silence. “Alright, alright — Limestone Pie, she…”

“She what?” Apple Bloom asked.
“She’s alienated everypony,” Marble Pie said softly. Apple Bloom sharpened her ears. “The night she became sure Maud and Mudbranch were dead, and the night Braeburn died, she grew more and more stubborn.”

“Braeburn?” Apple Bloom felt a chill.

“You know about him… everything,” Marble Pie whispered again, trying to deflect with ambiguity. Apple Bloom wouldn’t give her the escape. Apple Bloom’s eyes went wide. “No — I don’t know. Did Limestone Pie really murder him?”

Marble Pie hadn’t expected Apple Bloom to ask so bluntly; she flinched, then quickly covered Apple Bloom’s mouth. “It was an accident.”

Apple Bloom opened her mouth to press further, but Marble Pie’s ears had already drooped and she spoke first: “Still… she did go too far in this. To defeat the Empire, she was willing to sacrifice herself… and other ponies. I’ve warned her, but she no longer listens to anyone. She’s right about one thing — I’m always indecisive. You can’t blame her for that.”

Apple Bloom hugged her and said, “No — you’re the kindest pony I know… maybe the second kindest? Either way, you’re right.” Marble Pie fell silent. Apple Bloom continued, “Actually, I learned some things from Mossy Scent. I think every pony in the Apple Pie family should know the truth.”

Marble Pie froze. “That might… might not be a good idea,” she said fearfully. Apple Bloom shook her head. “The war is over and we haven’t won peace. If I can’t stop her, more innocent ponies will die. One day the whole Apple Pie family could wither. Many of our ponies already support her — we need to make Limestone Pie understand.”

Marble Pie stayed quiet for a long moment, then answered softly, “I… I can’t do anything. But… you must hurry. She won’t be away for long — seize the time.”

Apple Bloom readied to leave immediately. Suddenly Marble Pie grabbed her hoof.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_121_o0]
“Promise me — I don’t want any pony to get hurt because of this. Not even her.”

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_122]
Retaking Appleloosa

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_122_desc]
Without any prior notice or warning, when Apple Bloom came, panting heavily, to the funeral of an Apple family member, she startled everypony present.

Apple Bloom quickly scanned the scene. Mossy Scent and some ponies she had already contacted were there as well, and they exchanged a knowing glance.

“I have something to tell all of you,” Apple Bloom announced loudly as she ran to the priest.

Two hours later, she led dozens of Apple family members charging boldly into Appleloosa’s City Hall. The guards on duty, seeing this scene, neither dared to stop them nor ask questions. The only thing they could do was step aside.

Soon, before Apple Bloom could use Appleloosa’s broadcast tower to announce this astonishing news to all of Equestria, the Apple family members remaining in City Hall had already learned the truth: Braeburn’s death had not been caused by the Empire, but was instead an accident orchestrated by Limestone Pie.

Although some Apple family members hesitated, intimidated by Limestone’s authority, the majority rallied immediately. They quickly took control of the forces surrounding Appleloosa and declared that, until Limestone Pie explained the situation, Appleloosa would secede from Great Rockville.

That evening, when the flags of Great Rockville were lowered and the Apple family’s green star-apple banner was raised again, everypony in Appleloosa understood the significance. The old borders between Appleloosa and the quarry farm had begun an unprecedented tense standoff. The armies that had fought side by side yesterday were now instant adversaries.

At this moment, both sides waited for orders from their superiors. The future of the Apple Pie family was once again fractured because of Braeburn’s fate. What choice would Limestone Pie make next?

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_122_o0]
march to the sisters’ castles！

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_123]
Searching for Limestone

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_123_desc]
When Appleloosa declared its separation from Great Rockville, it seemed as if the nation’s soldiers had received no orders from Limestone Pie. Perhaps no ponies wished to see a civil war between the two families.

Yet, more and more members of the Apple Pie family joined Apple Bloom in her advance toward the sisters’ castle. They only wanted Limestone Pie to provide an explanation — a reasonable account of her previous actions. But there was nothing. The castle of the sisters remained utterly silent.

Now, Apple Bloom and Marble Pie once again walked through the halls of the sisters’ castle. No bloodshed had occurred during the takeover; Marble Pie had already come to the main gate to greet them. The other politicians merely had to sit quietly to ensure their own safety.

With a nervous heart, Apple Bloom pushed open the door to Limestone Pie’s office once more — only to find the room empty and in disarray.

For now, the most pressing matter was cleaning up the mess left behind by Limestone Pie. The family members held a brief council, and Apple Bloom was elected the temporary new leader, tasked with handling official affairs.

Most of the politicians within the castle soon returned to their positions. Only the generals were uncertain how to proceed. Apple Bloom told them to go home for the time being. Even if some wanted to seek out the now-missing Limestone Pie, Apple Bloom left it to their discretion.

Although she had learned little under Limestone Pie, Apple Bloom still tried to deal with the mountain of accumulated issues over the past few days. Beyond Limestone Pie’s whereabouts, her main concerns were whether she could gain Equestria's support, how illegally seized lands would be returned, and finally allowing the frontline soldiers to lay down their weapons.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_123_o0]
Where is she?

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_124]
A Ghost of the Pie Family

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_124_desc]
It had been a long time since the Appleloosa uprising — whether to call that movement an “uprising” at all was still up for debate. In any case, the international community gradually accepted that Limestone Pie had vanished, and they began to truly see Apple Bloom as the new voice of authority. The border forces had slowly returned to control; with Limestone Pie gone, even some of her supporters had accepted the new reality.

Although Apple Bloom still faced a lot of opposition, she led the Apple Pie family in redrafting its external policies and, under pressure, returned much land — especially Windferry and the Buffalo holdings. On the bright side, the Apple Pie family remained intact as an institution. The name “Greater Rockville” still gave Apple Bloom a headache: should it be renamed something like the “Apple Pie Republic”? She hadn’t decided.

While Apple Bloom stepped out briefly to fetch a glass of water, a letter inexplicably appeared on her desk. It bore Limestone Pie’s familiar mark. Apple Bloom steadied herself and opened the envelope.

“When you denounced my crimes on the air, I was furious. I could not understand why you treated me so. I even wanted to silence you by force as I have always done. But at the last moment I stopped — because I realized everything you said was true. Selfishly, to avoid facing the truth, I again pointed my gun at the ponies I loved most.

When your grandparents and your brothers and sisters passed away one after another, I felt I had nothing left to hold on to. I made revenge against the Empire the most important thing in my life. I believed that only when the Apple Pie family spoke with one voice could we win — win the victory I wanted. Do I regret that? That is complicated. Though it was accidental, I am glad I at least achieved an ignominious success.

Yet I betrayed a principle: we must not strike down our closest kin. If we do, how are we different from those we stand against? Now I have a real choice, and I will not make that mistake again. I know the Apple Pie family may refuse to accept me for a long time — perhaps forever. That is my punishment, and I accept it gladly.

Because of you, I have seen the future of our family and Ponyland in you. You are a symbol of light. If you overthrow me, soon every pony in the lands we govern will love you as they loved my sister. So I have decided to entrust the future of the Apple Pie family to you. I will go and truly see how ordinary ponies live.

Will I come back one day? That depends on you as well. Do not slack. I will watch everything from the shadow of the Apple Pie family — but for now, you are doing well.”

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_124_o0]
Signature: Sister Limestone, who loves You

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_124_TOOLTIP]
This is the end of her story. The PIHC production team thanks you for playing!

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_125]
Detained Loved Ones

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_125_desc]
Limestone Pie had always displayed her ruthlessness and firmness when showing herself publicly. Not long ago, she had almost lost her temper at the negotiating table with her former comrades. Yet now, she appeared slightly conflicted and embarrassed.

After a brief internal struggle, she saluted the standing guards and, accompanied by several soldiers, made her way through layers of barbed wire and security lines. Under the cover of night, they arrived at a remote base on the outskirts of Appleloosa.

Limestone Pie approached a door, signaling her soldiers to fall back. She knocked and then pushed it open, stepping inside.

“Bring me a cup of apple cider, with ice. And by the way, tell your Limestone Pie Supreme Commander that I’d like to know when she’s willing to pay a visit to her relatives,” said a stallion lurking in the shadows, his tone casual.

Limestone Pie lowered her head in slight guilt.

“Enough, Braeburn.”

The stallion slowly emerged from the shadows.

“What, haven’t you forgotten us yet? Wasn’t the victory feast against the Empire enough for you?”

“Listen, Braeburn, I’m not here to argue. I know I was too impulsive back then. I shouldn’t have kept you all here, but now the war is over. Under my leadership, we’ve won! Isn’t that enough?” Limestone Pie spoke in a tone of feigned pride.

She paused for a moment before continuing,

“We don’t need to remain enemies. I now… just want to reconcile. The Apple Pie family needs this.”

Her words came haltingly, and she didn’t understand why her voice sounded so much like her sister, Marble Pie.

“Oh? Now you bring up the family to justify yourself? Sure, you’ve won. Look around — your world doesn’t need us. Oh, yes… Long live Limestone Pie!” Braeburn shouted mockingly, his bright voice echoing around. Several pairs of eyes in the darkness scanned Limestone Pie back and forth, making her increasingly uncomfortable.

“You… no… all of this was for defeating the Empire, for the Apple Pie family, for our shared future!” Limestone Pie cried out incoherently, trying to mask her inner panic with anger.

“Listen, I want you to return to the Apple Pie family immediately. Everyone misses you, and you miss them, don’t you?”

Her words were met with silence.

“Peace has been achieved. I have no reason — yes, no reason — to keep you from showing yourselves. Forgive my previous actions. For the sake of defeating the Empire, we cannot have any division,” Limestone Pie pressed on, her voice brightening, her eyes full of expectation as she looked at Braeburn.

“You are right, dear. Our relatives miss us. But… when we go back, the Apple Pie family will cease to exist.”

“You? What do you mean?” Limestone Pie froze.

“As you said, peace has been achieved. The alliance between the Apple Pie family and the Pie family is no longer necessary. Therefore, we have decided to return Appleloosa to the control of the Apple family. Considering our past relations, I am willing to forgive your actions against our family during the war on behalf of the Apple family.”

“No! You… you can’t do this! We… together, we can create a new future!”

“Then we’d rather stay here. It makes no difference from now anyway.”

“You can’t do this to me! …To your loved ones!” Limestone Pie yelled at Braeburn.

Braeburn and the others remained silent. Limestone Pie gasped heavily, glared at Braeburn, and ground her teeth.

“Listen, I am sorry for what happened before. But since you haven’t made your decision today, I’ll give you some more time.”

She slammed the door shut.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_125_o0]
“And we will watch you from here, until you step into the abyss.”

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_126]
A private conversation

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_126_desc]
Apple Bloom clutched her head in pain, having just heard a completely different truth.

As a rising star of the Apple family, she had been completely unaware of what had happened within the Apple Pie family over the years while she and her friends were leading an uprising deep in the Empire’s territory.

When the war ended, she had expected to return home in glory — but she never imagined that everything here would be so different from the past.

Outside the window, the flag of Greater Rockville fluttered silently in the air. Mossy Scent wiped away her unstoppable tears, her mouth slightly open, wanting to say something comforting, but unable to find the words. In truth, she herself was the one who needed comfort the most.

She had just confessed everything: how she met Limestone Pie, how Limestone had asked her to assassinate Braeburn, and finally, how Limestone Pie had marched into Appleloosa. She had thought she would keep these secrets buried forever, or perhaps that revealing them might ease her conscience. But neither happened.

Now, the situation had far exceeded her imagination. As the one who set all this in motion, she knew she had to bear the responsibility.

Limestone Pie, in the name of both the Apple family and the Pie family, was turning her wrath toward one nation after another. Peace was like an apple hanging from a tree — always just within reach of her hoof, yet forever unattainable.

She had changed. So had Appleloosa, and the ponies working the land of the quarry farm.

At Braeburn’s recent public funeral, Limestone Pie had falsely recounted how her unwavering bond with him had been utterly destroyed by the Empire. In the crowd below, countless ponies shouted her name again and again. The scene made Mossy Scent feel even more nauseated and fearful.

She was grateful, at least, to still be alive — not locked away in a windowless cell under some strange charge by Rockville’s Bureau of Public Affairs. Perhaps this meant that Limestone Pie still trusted her not to reveal secrets… or perhaps Limestone truly saw her as family and a close friend.

“Are you saying… it was Limestone Pie who wanted to harm Braeburn, and even locked him away in some mysterious place?” Apple Bloom whispered hoarsely, her voice full of disbelief.

She looked at Mossy Scent with those sorrowful, wide eyes.
“I can’t believe Limestone would lie to me… but this isn’t your fault. At least… not yours alone.”

“No,” Mossy Scent said, trembling all over. “I know what I did. That one single choice… it led to everything that’s happening now.”

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_126_o0]
Now I just want to make up for this

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_126_TOOLTIP]
Apple Bloom will plan to rescue Braeburn

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_127]
An Invitation

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_127_desc]
After Mossy Scent temporarily returned, Apple Bloom compiled a list of the Apple Pie family members who were still present and those who were missing. To ensure the success of any potential plan, she could only approach a few trusted family members working in the government under the pretense of a visit, attempting to gain their support.

Although she still didn’t know the exact locations where Braeburn and the other ponies were being held, perhaps she could pick up some clues.

Today, however, when several sergeants arrived in front of Apple Bloom with an invitation, she was startled at first. But once she understood the situation, her panic deepened.

It turned out that Limestone Pie wanted her to represent the Apple family as an important member at a multi-species social banquet. In addition to the Apple Pie family, there would be parrots, buffalo, and ponies from some friendly nations.

In the invitation, Limestone Pie expressed how much she missed Apple Bloom. She longed for the warmth and joy of the nights by the stove in the quarry farm cabin with Apple Bloom and Applejack, and since the Empire was defeated, she hadn’t properly spoken with her most cherished sister.

Apple Bloom wasn’t ready to meet Limestone Pie again. But to avoid arousing suspicion, she decided to go anyway.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_127_o0]
hoped this wasn’t one of Limestone Pie’s schemes.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_127_TOOLTIP]
No matter what Apple Bloom was planning, she knew she would need even more patience…

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_128]
Braeburn’s Whereabouts

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_128_desc]
Apple Bloom was awakened by the noisy sounds outside. A pair of military vehicles, each equipped with steam engines, rumbled past the castle. These massive machines, except for not running on tracks, were much like trains.

She yawned and rolled off her soft bed. Glancing out the window, she noticed the moon still hanging in the sky, briefly reminding her of Princess Luna.

Pushing open the door, she saw many ponies rushing about, but still no sign of Limestone Pie. Apple Bloom knew who she needed to find.

By the time she found Marble Pie, the sun had already risen. From Marble Pie, she learned that the night before, Limestone Pie had launched a military operation against a neighboring nation, and she herself had gone to the front lines. Everypony in the castle was busy handling matters related to this.

“Aren’t you going? Why didn’t Sister Limestone take you along?” Apple Bloom asked, half-curiously.

Limestone Pie was silent for a moment before slowly replying,

“I’m not a pony skilled in command.”

“But according to rank, you’re still a general of Greater Rockville… the Apple Pie family,” Apple Bloom pressed.

“During the war, I was only responsible for logistics for the ponies. After the Empire fell, I gradually withdrew from the army…”

Apple Bloom didn’t continue questioning. She quietly watched Marble Pie.

“Alright, alright. Limestone Pie, she…”

“She what?”

“She has distanced herself from all of us,” Marble Pie whispered.

Apple Bloom perked up her ears.

“That night, when she was sure Maud Pie and Mudbranch had died, and that same night when Appleloosa was attacked… she became even more stubborn.”

“Attack Appleloosa?” Apple Bloom asked, though she already knew the answer.

“Those things… you already know,” Marble Pie muttered, shyly trying to evade the topic. But Apple Bloom didn’t give her the chance.

“No, I don’t. Did Limestone Pie really try to kill Brother Braeburn?”

Marble Pie was surprised by Apple Bloom’s bluntness. She quickly covered Apple Bloom’s mouth and whispered,

“No, Braeburn is still alive.”

Apple Bloom was about to ask further, but Marble Pie’s ears drooped, and she spoke first:

“But she was… rather extreme in this matter. To defeat the Empire, she was willing to sacrifice herself… and other ponies too. I tried to advise her, but she wouldn’t listen to anyone else. She was right in saying… I… I have always been indecisive. That’s not her fault.”

Apple Bloom hugged her and said,

“No, you are the kindest pony I’ve ever met… or maybe the second kindest. Either way, you are right.”

Marble Pie didn’t respond. Apple Bloom continued,

“Actually, I’ve learned some things from Mossy Scent and a few relatives. We must rescue Braeburn and the other relatives.”

Marble Pie froze.

“That… maybe… isn’t a good idea,” she said fearfully.

Apple Bloom shook her head.

“The war is over, but peace hasn’t come. If I can’t stop her, one day the entire Apple Pie family will turn to dead branches. Do you agree with what Limestone Pie is doing?”

Marble Pie was silent. After a brief pause, she whispered,

“They… they are all being held at that military base in the eastern outskirts of Appleloosa.”

Apple Bloom immediately prepared to leave. Suddenly, Marble Pie grabbed her hoof.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_128_o0]
“Promise me. I don’t want any pony to get hurt because of this… including her.”

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_129]
Retaking Appleloosa

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_129_desc]
There was no prior warning, and no sign of what was about to happen. Yet when Apple Bloom arrived, breathless, at a funeral for members of the Apple family, everypony present froze in surprise.

Apple Bloom quickly scanned the crowd. Mossy Scent and a few other ponies she had already reached out to beforehand were there. They exchanged a brief, knowing glance.

“I have something to tell everyone,” Apple Bloom called out loudly, running to the priest’s side.

Two hours later, she led dozens of Apple family members, charging boldly into the military base Marble Pie had mentioned. The guards on duty, witnessing the scene, neither dared stop them nor question their actions. All they could do was step aside and let them pass.

Soon, even the Apple family members still working at Appleloosa’s town hall learned the truth: Braeburn was alive, and the Apple Pie family was now reclaiming its legacy.

Although some members of the Apple family hesitated, intimidated by Limestone Pie’s authority, the majority mobilized swiftly, taking control of the surrounding Appleloosa forces.

By evening, when the flag of Great Rockville was lowered and the Apple family’s green-starred apple banner was raised once again, everypony in Appleloosa knew what it meant. The old borders between Appleloosa and the quarry farms had erupted into unprecedented tension. Armies that had fought side by side yesterday were suddenly adversaries.

Now, both forces waited for orders from their superiors. The future of the Apple Pie family hung in the balance once more, torn apart because of Braeburn.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_129_o0]
Was there still any way to salvage it all?

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_130]
ownership of the two sisters’ castle

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_130_desc]
Apple Bloom stepped off the train, closing her eyes and trying to catch the lingering scent of apples. Since the final war, she had left this place, journeying with her friends — the adorable scouts — in search of ways to resist the Empress. Many years had passed since then, and she had grown from a foal her age into a capable young mare, able to handle herself independently.

Through countless days and nights of guerrilla fighting deep in the forests or on the frontlines, she had always imagined this moment arriving.

Apple Bloom had read some news in the papers. She regretted missing Igneous Rock Pie’s and Cloudy Quartz’s funerals, but she still remembered them fondly — how they treated her like a granddaughter, and the delicious rock candy and rock cakes…

Yet it wasn’t too late. Her hometown still resembled her memories, though with many new skyscrapers. The streets no longer bore the flags of Appleloosa, but instead displayed the mark of her sister, Limestone Pie. It felt unfamiliar, yet acceptable.

She wanted to surprise Limestone Pie without revealing her whereabouts in advance. Limestone was one of the few relatives she still felt truly close to. Although Apple Bloom liked Pinkie Pie even more, those sorrowful memories were hard to revisit. The war had been won. If Pinkie Pie was still somewhere out there, if news from home could still reach her, she would surely be proud.

Apple Bloom wandered casually through the streets. Some ponies recognized her and waved their hooves — she hadn’t realized she had also become a war hero. Apple Bloom smiled wryly.

A few uniformed ponies spotted her and hurriedly ran toward the government building. Apple Bloom let out a soft chuckle; it seemed her surprise was no longer a secret.

As she curiously took in the changes of her hometown, a hoof suddenly grabbed her, pulling her into a quiet corner of the street. It was a serious yet warm face.

Apple Bloom recognized her: Mossy Scent, one of her distant relatives from the Apple Pie family.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_130_o0]
Mossy Scent led Apple Lily into her home.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_131]
Formation of the Troops

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_131_desc]
The forces in Appleloosa had already been reorganized under the control of the Apple Pie family members, with their units and affiliations redefined. A portion of the city’s citizens and military, who had resisted Limestone Pie, also declared their independence from Great Rockville and joined our ranks.

[en.EVENT_C12_MAIN_131_o0]
Yes!

